rred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/commits/be4059942c2abc8028385abecb95d2b3fdb0e1a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:56:10Z","email":"rajat1996kumar@gmail.com","name":"Rajat Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:56:10Z","email":"rajat1996kumar@gmail.com","name":"Rajat Kumar"},"message":"fix(kit,codemods): port agreement, outlet remounts, plugin adapters, CLI bin\n\nBugs found in the October 2026 project review, each with a regression test:\n\n- kit/vite: MFE and shell now share one port resolver. adapter.defaultPort\n  made an MFE serve where the shell never looked, and let two MFEs claim the\n  same port; it is now ignored and marked @deprecated in plugin-api.\n- kit: defineConfig rejects an MFE port equal to the shell''s (explicit or the\n  default 3000).\n- kit/react: inline `props={{...}}` no longer remounts the MFE on every parent\n  render (shallow-equal stabilizer; callbacks never compare equal).\n- kit/vite: config.plugins[].frameworkAdapters is honored (opts.adapters >\n  later plugins > earlier plugins > built-ins).\n- kit/vite: CSS-injection snippet is appended, keeping sourcemaps aligned.\n- codemods: mfkit-migrate compared argv[1] to import.meta.url verbatim and\n  silently no-op''d when launched through a .bin symlink/shim.\n\nThe example now relies on .tsx lifecycle inference instead of a hardcoded\nexposes map, so the e2e covers it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b05006fe13e47a331749678d2c8119c0eb8096db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/git/trees/b05006fe13e47a331749678d2c8119c0eb8096db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/git/commits/be4059942c2abc8028385abecb95d2b3fdb0e1a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35594926?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RJonMshka","id":35594926,"login":"RJonMshka","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTk0OTI2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/RJonMshka/mfkit/commit/be4059942c2abc8028385abecb95d2b3fdb0e1a6","node_id":"C_kwDOTEe9e9oAKGJlNDA1OTk0MmMyYWJjODAyODM4NWFiZWNiOTVkMmIzZmRiMGUxYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/RJonMshka/mfkit/commit/ef3bff7796f6011b2fc457dd36e75a6b694209ca","sha":"ef3bff7796f6011b2fc457dd36e75a6b694209ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/commits/ef3bff7796f6011b2fc457dd36e75a6b694209ca"}],"sha":"be4059942c2abc8028385abecb95d2b3fdb0e1a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/commits/be4059942c2abc8028385abecb95d2b3fdb0e1a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35594926?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RJonMshka","id":35594926,"login":"RJonMshka","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTk0OTI2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/commits/ef3bff7796f6011b2fc457dd36e75a6b694209ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T23:49:31Z","email":"rajat1996kumar@gmail.com","name":"Rajat Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T23:49:31Z","email":"rajat1996kumar@gmail.com","name":"Rajat Kumar"},"message":"chore: version packages (alpha)\n\n@mfkit/plugin-api, @mfkit/kit, @mfkit/codemods → 0.1.0-alpha.0.\n\nVersioned locally rather than via the changesets version-PR flow: that flow\nneeds GITHUB_TOKEN to open a PR, which on this repo would mean enabling\n\"Allow GitHub Actions to create and approve pull requests\" — a single toggle\nthat also lets Actions approve PRs, weakening the review gate on a public\nrepo. Publishing still happens in CI: with no changesets left pending, the\nRelease workflow goes straight to `changeset publish`.\n\nrelease.yml gets job-scoped `contents: write` / `pull-requests: write` so the\nchangesets action can push tags and create GitHub releases, while the\nrepo-wide default token stays read-only.\n\nThe examples are all `private: true`, so publish skips them despite the\nversion bumps.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"66c0dda21c894537ef3677f557ab5a5c66516826","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/git/trees/66c0dda21c894537ef3677f557ab5a5c66516826"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/git/commits/ef3bff7796f6011b2fc457dd36e75a6b694209ca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35594926?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RJonMshka","id":35594926,"login":"RJonMshka","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTk0OTI2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/RJonMshka/mfkit/commit/ef3bff7796f6011b2fc457dd36e75a6b694209ca","node_id":"C_kwDOTEe9e9oAKGVmM2JmZjc3OTZmNjAxMWIyZmM0NTdkZDM2ZTc1YTZiNjk0MjA5Y2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/RJonMshka/mfkit/commit/fdf2dfc80131859bfdc1179961e6eaa2576b5da7","sha":"fdf2dfc80131859bfdc1179961e6eaa2576b5da7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/commits/fdf2dfc80131859bfdc1179961e6eaa2576b5da7"}],"sha":"ef3bff7796f6011b2fc457dd36e75a6b694209ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/commits/ef3bff7796f6011b2fc457dd36e75a6b694209ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35594926?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RJonMshka","id":35594926,"login":"RJonMshka","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTk0OTI2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/commits/fdf2dfc80131859bfdc1179961e6eaa2576b5da7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T19:11:50Z","email":"rajat1996kumar@gmail.com","name":"Rajat Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T19:11:50Z","email":"rajat1996kumar@gmail.com","name":"Rajat Kumar"},"message":"fix(kit): close the four open DX findings from examples/minimal\n\nEverything here was surfaced by the first non-DevNexus consumer and is\nadopter-facing — an evaluator hits all four in their first hour.\n\n- Remote CSS never reached the shell. A built MFE extracts its styles into a\n  CSS asset referenced only by the remote''s own index.html, which a federated\n  host never loads, so every remote rendered unstyled in the shell while\n  looking correct standalone. mfkitMFE now folds the emitted CSS into the\n  remote''s entry chunks (src/vite/css-inject.ts) as an idempotent, non-throwing\n  <style> injection and drops the orphaned asset. `injectCss: false` opts out.\n  Dev was never affected — Vite serves styles over the module graph.\n\n- exposes hardcoded ./src/lifecycle.ts, so a React MFE (lifecycle is naturally\n  .tsx) failed deep inside the MF plugin with nothing pointing at the path kit\n  had invented. Kit now probes ./src/lifecycle.{ts,tsx,mts,js,jsx,mjs} and\n  throws an actionable MFKitConfigError when nothing matches. User-supplied\n  exposes is never probed. The probe checks both cwd and cwd + entry.path:\n  vite runs per-app, tooling runs from the workspace root, and manifest paths\n  are root-relative either way.\n\n- MFKitProvider churned its context on an inline `entries` array, remounting\n  every outlet when anything above the provider re-rendered. The entry map is\n  now keyed on content, not identity (createEntriesCache — pure, so it is\n  testable without a renderer, like the outlet controller). This also fixes a\n  latent bug found alongside it: the default quarantine registry was built\n  inside the memo, so invalidation handed out a fresh one and silently reset\n  failure counts — an MFE could never reach its quarantine threshold.\n\n- Generated federation configs pass `dts: false`. Kit owns remote types via\n  @mfkit/kit/types; the MF plugin''s dts machinery only added a\n  failed-to-prebundle warning to every dev boot.\n\nThe example''s e2e now asserts computed styles on the clock, not just mount\nstate — the CSS bug was invisible to every other assertion in it. Verified by\ndisabling injectCss and watching it fail with padding 0px.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1fd54d8ad105ea480b5d8d15d1c8df16af2f88e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/git/trees/1fd54d8ad105ea480b5d8d15d1c8df16af2f88e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RJonMshka/mfkit/git/commits/fdf2dfc80131859bfdc1179961e6eaa2576b5da7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35594926?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RJonMshka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.c