"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/commits/94f5c93b7d290ac35e77547c5da9aa08f3b9d301/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T06:04:57Z","email":"edwardlimkoksiong1994@gmail.com","name":"Edward Lim Kok Siong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T06:04:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: remove test1, test2, mfe1, web1 scaffolding (#78)\n\n* chore: remove test1, test2, mfe1, web1 scaffolding\n\nStrips the placeholder test1/test2 servers, mfe1/web1 frontends, and their\ngenerated API artifacts, CI/CD wiring, and Cypress e2e tests that referenced\nthem, now that real servers/frontends exist to replace them as examples.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: finish removing test1/test2/mfe1 scaffolding, regenerate lockfile\n\nThe prior commit dropped their generated API code and CI wiring but left\nservers/test1, servers/test2, and frontends/mfe1 tracked on disk. Their\nworkspace package.json files still depended on the now-deleted generated\npackages/api code, breaking `bun install` postinstall and failing CI''s\nlockfile check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: remove apps/web1 scaffolding, regenerate lockfile\n\nSame leftover as the prior test1/test2/mfe1 cleanup — apps/web1 was\nnamed in that commit''s message but never actually deleted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): add Query root to auth subgraph, fix supergraph composition\n\nauth became the apollo router''s only subgraph once test1/test2 were\nremoved from supergraph.yaml, but its schema only declared Mutation —\nfederation requires at least one subgraph to define a Query root, so\n`rover supergraph compose` failed with QUERY_ROOT_MISSING and\nservices/apollo''s INT-FEAT02-02 test failed CI. Added a trivial\nQuery.health field and regenerated packages/api.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: TapiruWanderCode94 <tapiruwandercode94@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c2befca9854f6efd9036341d8a44d864d801c9fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/git/trees/c2befca9854f6efd9036341d8a44d864d801c9fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/git/commits/94f5c93b7d290ac35e77547c5da9aa08f3b9d301","verification":{"payload":"tree c2befca9854f6efd9036341d8a44d864d801c9fb\nparent 1f33981a7033d08df4ae6d1f85c24963d23300b4\nauthor Edward Lim Kok Siong <edwardlimkoksiong1994@gmail.com> 1784095497 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784095497 +0800\n\nchore: remove test1, test2, mfe1, web1 scaffolding (#78)\n\n* chore: remove test1, test2, mfe1, web1 scaffolding\n\nStrips the placeholder test1/test2 servers, mfe1/web1 frontends, and their\ngenerated API artifacts, CI/CD wiring, and Cypress e2e tests that referenced\nthem, now that real servers/frontends exist to replace them as examples.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: finish removing test1/test2/mfe1 scaffolding, regenerate lockfile\n\nThe prior commit dropped their generated API code and CI wiring but left\nservers/test1, servers/test2, and frontends/mfe1 tracked on disk. Their\nworkspace package.json files still depended on the now-deleted generated\npackages/api code, breaking `bun install` postinstall and failing CI''s\nlockfile check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: remove apps/web1 scaffolding, regenerate lockfile\n\nSame leftover as the prior test1/test2/mfe1 cleanup — apps/web1 was\nnamed in that commit''s message but never actually deleted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): add Query root to auth subgraph, fix supergraph composition\n\nauth became the apollo router''s only subgraph once test1/test2 were\nremoved from supergraph.yaml, but its schema only declared Mutation —\nfederation requires at least one subgraph to define a Query root, so\n`rover supergraph compose` failed with QUERY_ROOT_MISSING and\nservices/apollo''s INT-FEAT02-02 test failed CI. Added a trivial\nQuery.health field and regenerated packages/api.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: TapiruWanderCode94 <tapiruwandercode94@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVyMJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf/AQABOZDV3DnRM72nPI3luTgIQB\n82N+p+MmZjaw2wUJK1t09dLg6OKsbDaLSkB3xXq7tQ1wLS+Xhl49009+JWF8i8pq\ncSCiPqkJaw0gvi0HJ36BjrvviZbA0IA2bPFAJYJkd3lUpzQW/v8ANOT8N1SpWsim\ntp/0xyour4UEEx/qcFOvklMQONG6Ta+jZB/uhApALYzAgMVSDEfOoBdbk5PWY4DS\nzFNwHTjPMTFFaAc3o9T8AC0hSfJBCkJJWXVJIdbfiOhGyJHgBs2Talt85TQGXkZT\nmko5s2miP2t1IEStoCB/GeH6Mut2aGUO/Eszq4bQvh9oZ75kWsRP8yunTgFeChdr\ngFBmewDsgzltHAiqzQ1pC6HFvIxUsVy8xk4yv1pjQasJpbrbZPmVxBKJIsb0xG+T\nrhoKbifzvsdJszV6+BuYPbZrlAiFCkwf/5t/Zg40hv3tdSaWAL/m1YEYYYP7fbNB\nxxxAyK/3n7mX5IygnaumMLX2LT+LnKTFCv5Opb3Kc4AVcDnISzD4atABV66UGr0y\n+MASjUdOmVdzsTRFcJARLff1ynub7gYvzn7CFjU4Rge5d+boM44YASZgxYlLztyI\nri5MlcRZkKA6HynSm2wtSqquCRuoOXYzvL99yHxD/BW15sX8YqyWFTLIoePzx9Fy\ne4G4dc7gfSPHgl/EesGK\n=gisu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T06:04:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"M