github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/commits/1f33981a7033d08df4ae6d1f85c24963d23300b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T13:52:35Z","email":"edwardlimkoksiong1994@gmail.com","name":"Edward Lim Kok Siong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T13:52:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): add ci-sonar-main.yml to re-scan main after every merge (#77)\n\nci-verify.yml only triggers on pull_request — main''s own SonarCloud branch analysis has never\nupdated after a merge throughout this repo''s history, since every scan that ever ran was\nPR-context analysis of some feature/bugfix/hotfix branch, never main itself. Confirmed hands-on\nthis session: querying `sonar list issues --branch main` kept returning results from whatever PR\nlast happened to touch main, not a fresh analysis reflecting the dozens of fixes just merged via\nthe SonarCloud-cleanup hotfix.\n\nNew workflow, not an added trigger on ci-verify.yml — that file''s concurrency group and its\n\"affected packages only\" test filter are both keyed off github.event.pull_request.*, which\ndoesn''t exist on a push event. ci-sonar-main.yml runs the full, unfiltered test suite (main''s\nown branch analysis needs real coverage across every package, not just whatever one PR touched)\nthen the same SonarCloud Scan action ci-verify.yml uses.\n\nAlso updates docs/src/content/docs/sdlc/ci-cd.mdx''s workflow-map table and SONAR_TOKEN''s\nconsumer list.","tree":{"sha":"3f87b8318fa02852223831c71f2225128274df0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/git/trees/3f87b8318fa02852223831c71f2225128274df0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/git/commits/1f33981a7033d08df4ae6d1f85c24963d23300b4","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f87b8318fa02852223831c71f2225128274df0a\nparent a906c09c89fa90b65464b07219c27d0c176c6070\nauthor Edward Lim Kok Siong <edwardlimkoksiong1994@gmail.com> 1784037155 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784037155 +0800\n\nfeat(ci): add ci-sonar-main.yml to re-scan main after every merge (#77)\n\nci-verify.yml only triggers on pull_request — main''s own SonarCloud branch analysis has never\nupdated after a merge throughout this repo''s history, since every scan that ever ran was\nPR-context analysis of some feature/bugfix/hotfix branch, never main itself. Confirmed hands-on\nthis session: querying `sonar list issues --branch main` kept returning results from whatever PR\nlast happened to touch main, not a fresh analysis reflecting the dozens of fixes just merged via\nthe SonarCloud-cleanup hotfix.\n\nNew workflow, not an added trigger on ci-verify.yml — that file''s concurrency group and its\n\"affected packages only\" test filter are both keyed off github.event.pull_request.*, which\ndoesn''t exist on a push event. ci-sonar-main.yml runs the full, unfiltered test suite (main''s\nown branch analysis needs real coverage across every package, not just whatever one PR touched)\nthen the same SonarCloud Scan action ci-verify.yml uses.\n\nAlso updates docs/src/content/docs/sdlc/ci-cd.mdx''s workflow-map table and SONAR_TOKEN''s\nconsumer list.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVj8jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoqgQAEskF4lNxYV2KKzin7IdQ95Z\nitmtH30fufdstqYC5ZLWF/ZUjTHG9+sEXKzaSYSPCWdnG5du8GTQKF9zxr3CkLLo\ni9XtKaD1YOKJdy/TVHaWNkELlFWsufcB+BX4C4xU4t9n9uIjs2R1HyHbwUv2ywlY\nvh9DF4NgPjSwInOTBMMF0z7ucFti6uz2OAblubzGStqreMKlU58elHw7NekibXW3\nRZixfeyB9bOwB5gA/FLocUCFCk0hXqAVqG1c1nOFKn6w8zVGwTSXgTSeCoG5VjRR\n4g1ZAQFc0feDS/8Cd+hY46z+Sy2NAj4YREv16mUoj9laDlmIAPgpW2SRs1r/vR+I\nDMD43D7+rMkhjd89/hrAD5eT4nlG2OKDjHcOsCgIZxH2b0GOg2U0RkYMmhxIUDIX\n12dzAYDP52DL7femsct/3Rmfd5l3sXMQy7mkgsrf8O9erVeRLW9O1q4Ws9RuLQvQ\nE/+aLMDc4ozgzEI+YwznQsvskXsfjRqRDGw3IZ2Uv2D+uDmN5R2OBk2