s{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/EdwardLim1994","id":50095107,"login":"EdwardLim1994","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDk1MTA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/commits/a906c09c89fa90b65464b07219c27d0c176c6070/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T13:39:45Z","email":"edwardlimkoksiong1994@gmail.com","name":"Edward Lim Kok Siong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T13:39:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[HOTFIX] 0.0.3 — SonarCloud quality gate cleanup (#73)\n\n* chore(openspec): add hotfix requirements for 0.0.3\n\n* [BUG] SonarCloud CRITICAL issues on main (cognitive complexity + empty methods) (#69)\n\n* refactor(server,turbo): resolve SonarCloud CRITICAL issues\n\n- CronRouter/KafkaRouter/GraphqlRouter: move the existing \"ponytail: no-op\"\n  explanation comment inside each empty register() body (S1186)\n- turbo/generators/helpers.ts: locale-aware sort in addNamedImport (S2871);\n  extract extractMobilePortFromPackageJson out of findAvailableMobilePort to\n  cut cognitive complexity (S3776)\n- GraphqlGenerator/GrpcGenerator: dedupe their near-identical\n  findAvailableGraphqlPort/findAvailableGrpcPort into a new shared\n  helpers.findAvailableServerPort, cutting both under the complexity\n  threshold (S3776)\n\nNo behavioural change — packages/server test suite (138 tests) still green.\n\n* fix(turbo): use String.raw in collectServerPortUsage regexes\n\nSonarCloud (typescript:S7780) flagged the new-code regex strings from the\nprior commit''s findAvailableServerPort extraction for double-escaping \\d/\\s\ninstead of using String.raw.\n\n* chore(sonar): exclude turbo/generators from coverage requirement\n\nnew_coverage quality gate condition was failing on this PR''s turbo/generators\nchanges (S2871/S3776/S7780 fixes) purely because turbo/generators has never\nhad a test runner wired up (not a workspace, no rstest.config.ts) — any line\ntouched there is unconditionally 0% covered. Same rationale as the existing\npackages/script/src/release exclusion: untested pre-existing tooling debt,\nnot product runtime code. Authorized explicitly by developer after gate\ninvestigation.\n\n* refactor(server): Strategy pattern for router registration (Registrable)\n\nReplaces the previous fix (moving the \"ponytail: no-op\" comment inside each\nempty register() body) with a real design fix for the same SonarCloud S1186\nfinding: CronRouter/KafkaConsumerRouter/GraphqlRouter never needed a\nregister() at all — only GrpcRouter does, since @grpc/grpc-js''s addService()\nis the sole way to attach a service to a Server, while CronDriver/KafkaDriver/\nApolloDriver read schedules/dispatchers, topics/dispatchers, and\ntypeDefs/resolvers directly.\n\n- New Registrable interface + isRegistrable() type guard\n  (packages/server/src/abstract/Registrable.ts)\n- BaseRouter is now a plain marker class — no register() member at all\n- GrpcRouter implements Registrable (its existing register() is unchanged)\n- CronRouter/KafkaConsumerRouter/GraphqlRouter: register() removed entirely,\n  not overridden\n- GrpcDriver now duck-types routers via isRegistrable() before calling\n  register(), matching ApolloDriver''s isGraphqlRouter/KafkaDriver''s\n  isKafkaConsumerRouter convention instead of assuming every router has it\n\n136/136 tests passing (net -2: removed 3 now-invalid \"register() is a no-op\"\ntests for routers that no longer have the method, added 1 covering\nGrpcDriver''s new skip-non-Registrable branch).\n\n* fix(k8s,turbo): resolve SonarCloud MAJOR issues (#70)\n\nKubernetes (24 Helm chart templates):\n- Add resources.requests (cpu/memory/ephemeral-storage) + resources.limits.memory to every\n  container missing them (S6892/S6873/S6864/S6897)\n- Add resources.limits.ephemeral-storage on the 12 containers backed by a PersistentVolumeClaim\n  (StatefulSet volumeClaimTemplates, or a Deployment mounting a PVC directly) — S6870\n- Add automountServiceAccountToken: false to every pod spec except traefik''s (which genuinely\n  needs its token — explicit serviceAccountName bound to ClusterRole/ClusterRoleBinding for the\n  Kubernetes Ingress provider) — S6865\n- Two conservative resource tiers: stateless (100m/128Mi requests, 256Mi memory limit) vs\n  PVC-backed (100m/256Mi requests, 512Mi memory limit) — sized for this local/dev deployment, not\n  production capacity planning\n- Verified: helm lint + helm template clean on all 14 touched charts\n\nTypeScript (turbo/generators, S8786 regex-superlinear-backtracking + S4624 nested template\nliteral + S6557 startsWith):\n- helpers.ts: new collapseTrailingNewlines() helper replaces repeated `raw.replace(/\\n+$/, ...)`\n  call sites (also used by DatabaseGenerator.ts/GraphqlGenerator.ts); injectDriverEntry''s\n  `.replace(/\\s*$/, \"\")` -> .trimEnd(); ensureComposeServiceListItems'' nested template literal\n  extracted to a separate itemLines variable\n- DatabaseGenerator.ts: injectServerAppChainCall''s `/^\\./.test(tail)` -> tail.startsWith(\".\");\n  injectVaultSecretEnvFrom''s two-line configMapRef marker regex replaced with plain substring\n  scanning (same behavior, no regex)\n- KafkaGenerator.ts: `.replace(/\\s*$/, \"\\n\")` -> `${...trimEnd()}\\n`\n- Verified all regex->string-method rewrites byte-identical to the original regex behavior\n  against a battery of edge-case inputs (empty string, no trailing newline, multiple trailing\n  newlines, whitespace-only, etc.)\n\nTwo pre-existing findings intentionally left as-is (token lacks issue-transition permissions to\nmark them reviewed in SonarCloud, and both are legitimate false positives / accepted risk, not\nreal code changes):\n- docker:S6596 on turbo/generators/templates/database/dockerfile-migrate-stage.hbs:5 — \"builder\"\n  is a prior Dockerfile build-stage name (FROM installer AS builder), not a pullable image; the\n  .hbs fragment is scanned standalone, out of Dockerfile context.\n- kubernetes:S5849 on services/vault/helm/templates/deployment.yaml:31 (IPC_LOCK) — required for\n  Vault to mlock() secrets in memory per HashiCorp''s own docs; removing it is less secure, not\n  more. Untouched line, so it doesn''t gate this PR''s new-code conditions.\n- kubernetes:S6596 on services/redis/helm/templates/statefulset.yaml (redis:latest) — already\n  documented as a deliberate exception in services/redis/CLAUDE.md (pinning breaks local dev due\n  to an RDB-format mismatch on the existing redis-data volume).\n\n* fix(turbo,script): resolve SonarCloud MINOR/INFO issues (#72)\n\n- turbo/generators/helpers.ts (8 sites), GraphqlGenerator.ts, CdcGenerator.ts: String.raw for\n  regex-literal template strings (S7780)\n- turbo/generators/helpers.ts: indexOf(...) !== -1 -> includes(...) in\n  ensureComposeNetworkDeclared (S7765)\n- turbo/generators/serverDriver/GrpcGenerator.ts: protoPackage''s replace(/-/g, \"_\") ->\n  replaceAll(\"-\", \"_\") (S7781)\n- packages/script/{generator/APIGenerator,helper/barrel}.ts: `import lodash from ''lodash''` ->\n  `import capitalize from ''lodash/capitalize''` (S8927)\n- turbo/generators/templates/mobile-project/src/app/index.tsx: HeroUILogo''s tintColor prop\n  marked readonly (S6759)\n- sonar-project.properties: exclude servers/*/generated/**/* (Prisma''s own generated client\n  output, same \"generated-only, never hand-edited\" category as the existing\n  packages/api/src/generated exclusion) — 5 findings there (S6582/S2094/S6635/S7772) were in\n  code nobody hand-edits\n\n~28 findings intentionally left open in SonarCloud (token lacks issue-transition permissions,\nsame wall as BUG-1/BUG-2, and none are real bugs):\n- 19x kubernetes:S5332/ansible:S5332/typescript:S5332 \"clear-text protocol\" — every instance is\n  an internal cluster-local or Docker-network hostname (vault.infra.svc.cluster.local,\n  kafka-connect:8083, schema-registry:8081, etc.), several already carrying their own \"never\n  actually dereferenced\"/\"reached from inside the Docker network, not from the host\" comments\n- 5x docker:S6471 \"runs as root\" — one-off Ansible provisioning tool containers (gated behind\n  the `tools` Compose profile, never in the running app''s request path), a third-party Confluent\n  base image, and the same dockerfile-migrate-stage.hbs template-fragment false positive already\n  documented in BUG-2''s PR (FROM builder AS migrate — builder is a prior stage name, not a\n  pullable image; scanning the .hbs fragment standalone loses that context)\n- 6x terraform:S1135 TODO comments — deliberately deferred real-cloud-backend bucket/region\n  choice (services/terraform/providers.tf, terraform/providers.tf), not a forgotten task\n- 3x typescript:S1874 \"''name'' is deprecated\" on `<h1>{{ name }}</h1>` in three frontend scaffold\n  templates — {{ name }} is a Handlebars placeholder (turbo/generators/helpers.ts''s\n  copyWithSubstitutions convention), not real JSX; scanned standalone it parses as a JSX\n  expression container referencing the browser''s deprecated global `name`\n- typescript:S1128 \"unused import\" on frontends/mfe1/src/router.tsx — already false: both\n  createRoute and Outlet are used in the current file. Stale SonarCloud data (ci-verify.yml only\n  scans on pull_request, so main''s last recorded analysis predates whatever PR actually fixed\n  this) — no code change made since there''s nothing to fix.\n\nAll fixes verified: tsc --noEmit clean, packages/server (136 tests) + packages/script suites\npassing.\n\n* fix(ci): support multi-app hotfixes in cd-hotfix.yml (#74)\n\ncd-hotfix.yml enforced exactly one touched deployable app per hotfix branch, hard-failing\notherwise. That assumption held for a classic single-bug hotfix, but broke on this SonarCloud\nquality-gate hotfix (0.0.3), which legitimately spans 5 apps (test1, auth, test2, mfe1, web1) —\nconfirmed harmless in practice (4/4 prior pushes to hotfix/0.0.3-sonarqube-quality-gate failed at\nthe same \"Identify the touched app\" step, before build-and-push/terraform-apply-prod ever ran —\nzero prod impact from any of them).\n\n- \"Identify the touched app(s)\" now only fails on zero touched apps, not >1\n- Version-bump step loops release_manager.sh.ts''s existing single-app `hotfix <app>` command once\n  per touched app (no changes to packages/script/src/release/ReleaseManager.ts itself), collecting\n  results into one JSON array job output\n- build-and-push becomes a matrix job over that array — one image build+push per app, fully\n  independent, safe to parallelize\n- terraform-apply-prod stays a single (non-matrixed) job: one `terraform apply` with one\n  -target=module.<name>/-var=<name>_app_image_tag=<version> pair per touched app. Matrixing this\n  one would race multiple applies against the same state file/lock instead of composing cleanly\n  the way the independent per-app image builds do.\n\nVerified: YAML parses (js-yaml), the jq/bash aggregation logic dry-run against simulated 5-app,\n1-app, and 0-app inputs all produce the expected output/error, and every touched app''s name\nmatches both its terraform/main.tf module name and terraform/variables.tf''s\n<name>_app_image_tag variable exactly.\n\nAlso updates docs/src/content/docs/sdlc/ci-cd.mdx''s workflow-map table and release:touched-apps\ndescription, which both still described the old single-app-only behavior.\n\n* fix(ci): compact touched-apps JSON before writing to GITHUB_OUTPUT (#75)\n\nrelease_manager.sh.ts pretty-prints its JSON output (JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)) — the\n\"Identify the touched apps\" step wrote that multi-line string directly as apps=$apps, which\nGITHUB_OUTPUT''s file-command format rejects: every line after the first gets parsed as its own\nmalformed \"key=value\" pair (\"Invalid format ''  \\\"test1\\\",''\"), not as part of one value.\n\nPipe through `jq -c ''.''` to compact to a single line first, same as the later \"Bump each touched\napp''s patch version\" step already does for its own `apps` output. Verified locally: simulated the\nexact multi-line input, confirmed the old code produced a 6-line file (breaking $GITHUB_OUTPUT''s\none-key-value-pair-per-line contract) and the fix produces exactly 1 line.\n\n* chore: :wrench: Add initial version of new apps\n\n* chore: :wrench: Update initial version to 0.0.1\n\n* fix(script): log.success to stderr, not stdout — fixes cd-hotfix.yml''s jq parse (#76)\n\nrelease_manager.sh.ts''s release:* commands (cut-release/bump-rc/promote/hotfix) each call\nlog.success(...) once per touched app, then print a final JSON result to stdout for the calling\nshell to capture. With log.success on console.log, that per-app success line landed on the same\nstream ahead of the JSON — cd-hotfix.yml''s `result=$(bun ... hotfix \"$app\")` then fed\n\"[SUCCESS]: ...\\n{...}\" straight into `jq --argjson`, which rejects a value with leading\nnon-JSON text (\"invalid JSON text passed to --argjson\"). This bug predates the multi-app\nrewrite — the original single-app flow would have hit the same thing, it just never reached\nthis step in any observed run (every prior run failed earlier, at the exactly-one-app check).\n\nlog.warn/log.error already used console.warn/console.error; only log.info/log.success used\nconsole.log. Moving log.success alone to console.error is the minimal fix matching the actual\ncollision — ReleaseManager''s release:* methods only ever call log.success, never log.info, so\nthat''s the only one whose stdout output collides with the final JSON print.\n\nVerified: packages/script suite (38 tests) passing, and manually confirmed via a real bun\ninvocation that stdout now contains only the JSON (parses cleanly with `jq .`) while\n\"[SUCCESS]: ...\" lands on stderr.\n\n* chore(hotfix): bump test1@1.1.1, auth@1.1.1, test2@1.1.1, mfe1@1.1.1, web1@1.1.1 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"fc20e414a32dc6af1577677c6bc23d45db0f8898","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/git/trees/fc20e414a32dc6af1577677c6bc23d45db0f8898"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/git/commits/a906c09c89fa90b65464b07219c27d0c176c6070","verification":{"payload":"tree fc20e414a32dc6af1577677c6bc23d45db0f8898\nparent ac1cf83f5bdb3235fc9b8db7c577179004ed68f2\nauthor Edward Lim Kok Siong <edwardlimkoksiong1994@gmail.com> 1784036385 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784036385 +0800\n\n[HOTFIX] 0.0.3 — SonarCloud quality gate cleanup (#73)\n\n* chore(openspec): add hotfix requirements for 0.0.3\n\n* [BUG] SonarCloud CRITICAL issues on main (cognitive complexity + empty methods) (#69)\n\n* refactor(server,turbo): resolve SonarCloud CRITICAL issues\n\n- CronRouter/KafkaRouter/GraphqlRouter: move the existing \"ponytail: no-op\"\n  explanation comment inside each empty register() body (S1186)\n- turbo/generators/helpers.ts: locale-aware sort in addNamedImport (S2871);\n  extract extractMobilePortFromPackageJson out of findAvailableMobilePort to\n  cut cognitive complexity (S3776)\n- GraphqlGenerator/GrpcGenerator: dedupe their near-identical\n  findAvailableGraphqlPort/findAvailableGrpcPort into a new shared\n  helpers.findAvailableServerPort, cutting both under the complexity\n  threshold (S3776)\n\nNo behavioural change — packages/server test suite (138 tests) still green.\n\n* fix(turbo): use String.raw in collectServerPortUsage regexes\n\nSonarCloud (typescript:S7780) flagged the new-code regex strings from the\nprior commit''s findAvailableServerPort extraction for double-escaping \\d/\\s\ninstead of using String.raw.\n\n* chore(sonar): exclude turbo/generators from coverage requirement\n\nnew_coverage quality gate condition was failing on this PR''s turbo/generators\nchanges (S2871/S3776/S7780 fixes) purely because turbo/generators has never\nhad a test runner wired up (not a workspace, no rstest.config.ts) — any line\ntouched there is unconditionally 0% covered. Same rationale as the existing\npackages/script/src/release exclusion: untested pre-existing tooling debt,\nnot product runtime code. Authorized explicitly by developer after gate\ninvestigation.\n\n* refactor(server): Strategy pattern for router registration (Registrable)\n\nReplaces the previous fix (moving the \"ponytail: no-op\" comment inside each\nempty register() body) with a real design fix for the same SonarCloud S1186\nfinding: CronRouter/KafkaConsumerRouter/GraphqlRouter never needed a\nregister() at all — only GrpcRouter does, since @grpc/grpc-js''s addService()\nis the sole way to attach a service to a Server, while CronDriver/KafkaDriver/\nApolloDriver read schedules/dispatchers, topics/dispatchers, and\ntypeDefs/resolvers directly.\n\n- New Registrable interface + isRegistrable() type guard\n  (packages/server/src/abstract/Registrable.ts)\n- BaseRouter is now a plain marker class — no register() member at all\n- GrpcRouter implements Registrable (its existing register() is unchanged)\n- CronRouter/KafkaConsumerRouter/GraphqlRouter: register() removed entirely,\n  not overridden\n- GrpcDriver now duck-types routers via isRegistrable() before calling\n  register(), matching ApolloDriver''s isGraphqlRouter/KafkaDriver''s\n  isKafkaConsumerRouter convention instead of assuming every router has it\n\n136/136 tests passing (net -2: removed 3 now-invalid \"register() is a no-op\"\ntests for routers that no longer have the method, added 1 covering\nGrpcDriver''s new skip-non-Registrable branch).\n\n* fix(k8s,turbo): resolve SonarCloud MAJOR issues (#70)\n\nKubernetes (24 Helm chart templates):\n- Add resources.requests (cpu/memory/ephemeral-storage) + resources.limits.memory to every\n  container missing them (S6892/S6873/S6864/S6897)\n- Add resources.limits.ephemeral-storage on the 12 containers backed by a PersistentVolumeClaim\n  (StatefulSet volumeClaimTemplates, or a Deployment mounting a PVC directly) — S6870\n- Add automountServiceAccountToken: false to every pod spec except traefik''s (which genuinely\n  needs its token — explicit serviceAccountName bound to ClusterRole/ClusterRoleBinding for the\n  Kubernetes Ingress provider) — S6865\n- Two conservative resource tiers: stateless (100m/128Mi requests, 256Mi memory limit) vs\n  PVC-backed (100m/256Mi requests, 512Mi memory limit) — sized for this local/dev deployment, not\n  production capacity planning\n- Verified: helm lint + helm template clean on all 14 touched charts\n\nTypeScript (turbo/generators, S8786 regex-superlinear-backtracking + S4624 nested template\nliteral + S6557 startsWith):\n- helpers.ts: new collapseTrailingNewlines() helper replaces repeated `raw.replace(/\\n+$/, ...)`\n  call sites (also used by DatabaseGenerator.ts/GraphqlGenerator.ts); injectDriverEntry''s\n  `.replace(/\\s*$/, \"\")` -> .trimEnd(); ensureComposeServiceListItems'' nested template literal\n  extracted to a separate itemLines variable\n- DatabaseGenerator.ts: injectServerAppChainCall''s `/^\\./.test(tail)` -> tail.startsWith(\".\");\n  injectVaultSecretEnvFrom''s two-line configMapRef marker regex replaced with plain substring\n  scanning (same behavior, no regex)\n- KafkaGenerator.ts: `.replace(/\\s*$/, \"\\n\")` -> `${...trimEnd()}\\n`\n- Verified all regex->string-method rewrites byte-identical to the original regex behavior\n  against a battery of edge-case inputs (empty string, no trailing newline, multiple trailing\n  newlines, whitespace-only, etc.)\n\nTwo pre-existing findings intentionally left as-is (token lacks issue-transition permissions to\nmark them reviewed in SonarCloud, and both are legitimate false positives / accepted risk, not\nreal code changes):\n- docker:S6596 on turbo/generators/templates/database/dockerfile-migrate-stage.hbs:5 — \"builder\"\n  is a prior Dockerfile build-stage name (FROM installer AS builder), not a pullable image; the\n  .hbs fragment is scanned standalone, out of Dockerfile context.\n- kubernetes:S5849 on services/vault/helm/templates/deployment.yaml:31 (IPC_LOCK) — required for\n  Vault to mlock() secrets in memory per HashiCorp''s own docs; removing it is less secure, not\n  more. Untouched line, so it doesn''t gate this PR''s new-code conditions.\n- kubernetes:S6596 on services/redis/helm/templates/statefulset.yaml (redis:latest) — already\n  documented as a deliberate exception in services/redis/CLAUDE.md (pinning breaks local dev due\n  to an RDB-format mismatch on the existing redis-data volume).\n\n* fix(turbo,script): resolve SonarCloud MINOR/INFO issues (#72)\n\n- turbo/generators/helpers.ts (8 sites), GraphqlGenerator.ts, CdcGenerator.ts: String.raw for\n  regex-literal template strings (S7780)\n- turbo/generators/helpers.ts: indexOf(...) !== -1 -> includes(...) in\n  ensureComposeNetworkDeclared (S7765)\n- turbo/generators/serverDriver/GrpcGenerator.ts: protoPackage''s replace(/-/g, \"_\") ->\n  replaceAll(\"-\", \"_\") (S7781)\n- packages/script/{generator/APIGenerator,helper/barrel}.ts: `import lodash from ''lodash''` ->\n  `import capitalize from ''lodash/capitalize''` (S8927)\n- turbo/generators/templates/mobile-project/src/app/index.tsx: HeroUILogo''s tintColor prop\n  marked readonly (S6759)\n- sonar-project.properties: exclude servers/*/generated/**/* (Prisma''s own generated client\n  output, same \"generated-only, never hand-edited\" category as the existing\n  packages/api/src/generated exclusion) — 5 findings there (S6582/S2094/S6635/S7772) were in\n  code nobody hand-edits\n\n~28 findings intentionally left open in SonarCloud (token lacks issue-transition permissions,\nsame wall as BUG-1/BUG-2, and none are real bugs):\n- 19x kubernetes:S5332/ansible:S5332/typescript:S5332 \"clear-text protocol\" — every instance is\n  an internal cluster-local or Docker-network hostname (vault.infra.svc.cluster.local,\n  kafka-connect:8083, schema-registry:8081, etc.), several already carrying their own \"never\n  actually dereferenced\"/\"reached from inside the Docker network, not from the host\" comments\n- 5x docker:S6471 \"runs as root\" — one-off Ansible provisioning tool containers (gated behind\n  the `tools` Compose profile, never in the running app''s request path), a third-party Confluent\n  base image, and the same dockerfile-migrate-stage.hbs template-fragment false positive already\n  documented in BUG-2''s PR (FROM builder AS migrate — builder is a prior stage name, not a\n  pullable image; scanning the .hbs fragment standalone loses that context)\n- 6x terraform:S1135 TODO comments — deliberately deferred real-cloud-backend bucket/region\n  choice (services/terraform/providers.tf, terraform/providers.tf), not a forgotten task\n- 3x typescript:S1874 \"''name'' is deprecated\" on `<h1>{{ name }}</h1>` in three frontend scaffold\n  templates — {{ name }} is a Handlebars placeholder (turbo/generators/helpers.ts''s\n  copyWithSubstitutions convention), not real JSX; scanned standalone it parses as a JSX\n  expression container referencing the browser''s deprecated global `name`\n- typescript:S1128 \"unused import\" on frontends/mfe1/src/router.tsx — already false: both\n  createRoute and Outlet are used in the current file. Stale SonarCloud data (ci-verify.yml only\n  scans on pull_request, so main''s last recorded analysis predates whatever PR actually fixed\n  this) — no code change made since there''s nothing to fix.\n\nAll fixes verified: tsc --noEmit clean, packages/server (136 tests) + packages/script suites\npassing.\n\n* fix(ci): support multi-app hotfixes in cd-hotfix.yml (#74)\n\ncd-hotfix.yml enforced exactly one touched deployable app per hotfix branch, hard-failing\notherwise. That assumption held for a classic single-bug hotfix, but broke on this SonarCloud\nquality-gate hotfix (0.0.3), which legitimately spans 5 apps (test1, auth, test2, mfe1, web1) —\nconfirmed harmless in practice (4/4 prior pushes to hotfix/0.0.3-sonarqube-quality-gate failed at\nthe same \"Identify the touched app\" step, before build-and-push/terraform-apply-prod ever ran —\nzero prod impact from any of them).\n\n- \"Identify the touched app(s)\" now only fails on zero touched apps, not >1\n- Version-bump step loops release_manager.sh.ts''s existing single-app `hotfix <app>` command once\n  per touched app (no changes to packages/script/src/release/ReleaseManager.ts itself), collecting\n  results into one JSON array job output\n- build-and-push becomes a matrix job over that array — one image build+push per app, fully\n  independent, safe to parallelize\n- terraform-apply-prod stays a single (non-matrixed) job: one `terraform apply` with one\n  -target=module.<name>/-var=<name>_app_image_tag=<version> pair per touched app. Matrixing this\n  one would race multiple applies against the same state file/lock instead of composing cleanly\n  the way the independent per-app image builds do.\n\nVerified: YAML parses (js-yaml), the jq/bash aggregation logic dry-run against simulated 5-app,\n1-app, and 0-app inputs all produce the expected output/error, and every touched app''s name\nmatches both its terraform/main.tf module name and terraform/variables.tf''s\n<name>_app_image_tag variable exactly.\n\nAlso updates docs/src/content/docs/sdlc/ci-cd.mdx''s workflow-map table and release:touched-apps\ndescription, which both still described the old single-app-only behavior.\n\n* fix(ci): compact touched-apps JSON before writing to GITHUB_OUTPUT (#75)\n\nrelease_manager.sh.ts pretty-prints its JSON output (JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)) — the\n\"Identify the touched apps\" step wrote that multi-line string directly as apps=$apps, which\nGITHUB_OUTPUT''s file-command format rejects: every line after the first gets parsed as its own\nmalformed \"key=value\" pair (\"Invalid format ''  \\\"test1\\\",''\"), not as part of one value.\n\nPipe through `jq -c ''.''` to compact to a single line first, same as the later \"Bump each touched\napp''s patch version\" step already does for its own `apps` output. Verified locally: simulated the\nexact multi-line input, confirmed the old code produced a 6-line file (breaking $GITHUB_OUTPUT''s\none-key-value-pair-per-line contract) and the fix produces exactly 1 line.\n\n* chore: :wrench: Add initial version of new apps\n\n* chore: :wrench: Update initial version to 0.0.1\n\n* fix(script): log.success to stderr, not stdout — fixes cd-hotfix.yml''s jq parse (#76)\n\nrelease_manager.sh.ts''s release:* commands (cut-release/bump-rc/promote/hotfix) each call\nlog.success(...) once per touched app, then print a final JSON result to stdout for the calling\nshell to capture. With log.success on console.log, that per-app success line landed on the same\nstream ahead of the JSON — cd-hotfix.yml''s `result=$(bun ... hotfix \"$app\")` then fed\n\"[SUCCESS]: ...\\n{...}\" straight into `jq --argjson`, which rejects a value with leading\nnon-JSON text (\"invalid JSON text passed to --argjson\"). This bug predates the multi-app\nrewrite — the original single-app flow would have hit the same thing, it just never reached\nthis step in any observed run (every prior run failed earlier, at the exactly-one-app check).\n\nlog.warn/log.error already used console.warn/console.error; only log.info/log.success used\nconsole.log. Moving log.success alone to console.error is the minimal fix matching the actual\ncollision — ReleaseManager''s release:* methods only ever call log.success, never log.info, so\nthat''s the only one whose stdout output collides with the final JSON print.\n\nVerified: packages/script suite (38 tests) passing, and manually confirmed via a real bun\ninvocation that stdout now contains only the JSON (parses cleanly with `jq .`) while\n\"[SUCCESS]: ...\" lands on stderr.\n\n* chore(hotfix): bump test1@1.1.1, auth@1.1.1, test2@1.1.1, mfe1@1.1.1, web1@1.1.1 [skip ci]","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVjwhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbJMQADHZodNy8t6qCASIZPDXTLK1\nhXMU5Tu5GJh31bC+ebNxbNJSjaTuxppy0IOxC22u2AVFQSsO7QWfuNR7Ged8Wa8f\nbKU56wbK+11Z3k738eqqadm+ey5k41mHbXmcN4gDlQAqZqX31iwwj/zyXea2A0Ta\n+A6+EnrEhJ/ohYEarslU9GhMDuP3u+onDVyYZopVxz1rBNuB2vGl94sD1yRhq1OL\nXroDhkFr2Vku+otJxpqt5A4QTxTY17Xl0g2irKW8idVBs8NPZ7qv+MAU3Uotj+GS\n1O0nM/FE9ZbmY69eH4lWsVKZ9Npy2gT2TKQAagqxxUSkI5WHDK/ObklSO+ZesPGC\nu34u+9UEJh2FYe8gJteDBM6ynfTL7j48eoP5vL3nPrRb/1YQ5rsEYRpc8hSTSxhh\n5rAsnQZk972BLWkfMdS/HmWH+SyFsvAGIi5dOytBJIV3USzBaB6rzu/gpl8oVDUQ\nI0oNIGwluNJ/hPYyDyoWzknvZA1NIGGuwE30y3ScslBPtjSAxfyUhUfezVTTounG\nDKmCeX03UZ2Vo5BicwFr5srZG+C5udTKTqic8wNJHuth3u5QUM0x+hY3KmTCeFbZ\nvCXozoisIeFquYJEPrVatSazSeyt69irxYhtuHlMRDxgf/1fNpST1HQflTZz7NAu\n/IsGiwYJalT80HyeXSxD\n=aE/z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T13:39:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.g