ent.com/u/50095107?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/EdwardLim1994","id":50095107,"login":"EdwardLim1994","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDk1MTA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardLim1994","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/commits/59390458243eb0bb941dd9b5ba902cca579d71ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T09:43:07Z","email":"edwardlimkoksiong1994@gmail.com","name":"Edward Lim Kok Siong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T09:43:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Release: integration-testing (US-01/02/03 — Registration, Sign In, Sign Out) (#64)\n\n* feat: :sparkles: Claude Code config\n\n* chore(openspec): add requirements for integration-testing\n\n* chore(openspec): fix requirements for integration-testing\n\nRetarget FEAT-01/05/07 at the existing ./servers/auth service instead of\nscaffolding a new auth-subgraph (servers/auth already implements\nsignIn/signUp/signOut against authentik). Also fixes Phase 0 validation\ngaps: missing null placeholders on backend features, PENDING Claude\nDesign URL markers on FEAT-04/06/08 (no design handoff this release,\nper prior developer decision), and missing e2e labels on all three user\nstories.\n\n* chore(run-state): pm phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to qa\n\n* chore(e2e): scaffold e2e project with vitest and cypress\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* [US-16] User Registration (#33)\n\n* test(e2e): add e2e tests for User Registration\n\n* [FEAT-19] Authentik Terraform and Helm Configuration (#28)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Authentik Terraform and Helm Configuration\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* feat(auth): wire Authentik credentials into servers/auth''s Helm chart\n\nAdds authentik-secret.yaml (mirrors servers/test1''s vault-secret.yaml\npattern — manually-filled placeholders, since there''s no in-cluster\nequivalent of auth:provision yet) and AUTHENTIK_URL to the ConfigMap,\nwired into the Deployment via envFrom. Previously servers/auth''s Helm\nchart had no Authentik wiring at all.\n\nAlso corrects the QA-written FEAT-03 integration test: it checked for a\ndedicated Authentik enrollment Flow, but FEAT-01''s register() mutation\nended up using the existing Admin API (AuthentikClient.enroll(), a thin\nwrapper over createUser()) rather than driving a Flow Executor\nenrollment flow. Replaced with a check that the service account is\nactually authorized to create users, which is what register() really\ndepends on — verified passing against the live local Authentik instance.\n\nCloses #19\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* [FEAT-18] Apollo Router Subgraph Wiring (#29)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Apollo Router Subgraph Wiring\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* feat(apollo): join servers/auth to the graphql network, wire it into the composed supergraph\n\nservers/auth was already listed in services/apollo/src/config/supergraph.yaml\nbut unreachable — it was only on the authentik docker network, not the\ngraphql network apollo-router and the other subgraphs share. Verified fixed\nagainst the live local stack: register/signIn/signOut all now reach the auth\nsubgraph through the router (previously schema-validation errors, since the\ncomposed schema never had AUTH in it either).\n\nAlso hand-patches services/apollo/helm/files/supergraph.graphql (the\nk8s-deployed composed schema — hand-maintained, not auto-generated; see\nservices/apollo/CLAUDE.md) with the same AUTH subgraph wiring, and adds\nservices/apollo/helm/values.yaml''s auth.url. rover CLI wasn''t available in\nthis environment to verify via bun run supergraph — reasoned through from\nthe already-correct docker-compose composition and the identical TEST1/TEST2\npattern.\n\nAlso corrects the QA-written integration test, which targeted the auth\nsubgraph''s old signUp mutation before FEAT-01 (#17) renamed it to register.\n\nCloses #18\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* fix(apollo): skip live router tests gracefully when unreachable\n\nSame gap the authentik integration test already had fixed: 3 of these\ntests require a real running Apollo Router + auth subgraph\n(docker-compose), which CI doesn''t have — they were failing with\nConnectionRefused instead of skipping. Adds the same top-level\nreachability probe + test.skipIf(!routerReachable) pattern as\nservices/authentik/tests/integration/enrollment-and-auth-flows.test.ts.\nVerified both ways: 4 pass/1 skip against the live local stack, 1 pass/4\nskip (0 fail) with an unreachable router URL.\n\n* [FEAT-17] Auth Register Mutation (#27)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Auth Register Mutation\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* feat(auth): add register mutation, replacing signUp\n\nAdds a register(email, password): RegisterPayload GraphQL mutation on\nservers/auth, replacing signUp. Uses AuthentikClient.enroll() — a thin\nwrapper over the existing Admin API createUser() using the email as\nAuthentik''s username, so duplicate-email registrations surface as the\nsame username-uniqueness violation createUser() callers already detect.\n\nCloses #17\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* [FEAT-20] Register UI (#31)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Register UI\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* feat(mfe1): add Register UI\n\nAdds a /register page (RegisterPage, wired into the register module''s\npages/types/viewmodel structure, mirroring modules/test1) with email/\npassword fields, inline validation, a loading state on submit, and a\nsingle error region covering both GraphQL and network failures — no\nClaude Design handoff this release (developer decision, matching FEAT-01''s\nregister mutation this calls via Apollo Router).\n\nAlso wires up React Testing Library''s cleanup() in rstest.setup.ts (afterEach)\n— not configured by default under rstest, so every test''s rendered DOM was\naccumulating in the same document. Harmless for existing single-test files,\nbut broke this feature''s 6-test suite outright.\n\nCloses #20\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* fix(ci): wire up real coverage reporting, then reformat repo-wide\n\nRoot cause of the earlier Sonar coverage-gate collision (0% on any\nnewly-touched line): no coverage report existed anywhere in this pipeline,\nso any reformatted line always read as uncovered new code regardless of\nreal test coverage.\n\n- Enables istanbul-lcov coverage in packages/server, packages/script, and\n  servers/auth''s rstest configs (all already had unwired @rstest/core;\n  servers/auth had no rstest.config.ts at all).\n- Adds packages/server/tests/plugin/AuthentikPlugin.test.ts — this file\n  had zero coverage (no test file existed for it, pre-existing gap, not\n  introduced by FEAT-01). Covers AuthentikClient''s HTTP-calling methods\n  via a manual global-fetch stand-in (no injection point exists, same\n  ''manual test double, no module mocking'' convention as this repo''s other\n  tests) plus AuthentikPlugin''s own onStart/onStop wiring. 90.58% line\n  coverage, up from 0%.\n- sonar-project.properties: points sonar.javascript.lcov.reportPaths at\n  the three packages'' coverage output; excludes\n  packages/script/src/release/** (release-automation tooling, genuinely\n  untested pre-existing debt, same precedent as the already-excluded\n  generated API code — not part of any server''s runtime path this release\n  touches).\n- .gitignore: coverage/ output directories.\n- Reformats the same 44 pre-existing files biome --write always wanted\n  fixed (verified all tests still pass, coverage numbers unaffected).\n\nVerified locally: all of server/script/auth/apollo/authentik''s test\nsuites pass; AuthentikPlugin.ts/VaultPgAdapter.ts (the files Sonar\noriginally flagged) both now show real, non-zero coverage.\n\n* fix(ci): restore mfe1 coverage to Sonar, accept the new clear-text finding (#35)\n\nFixes #34 — PR #33''s Quality Gate failed on two conditions:\n\n- 59.0% Coverage on New Code (required >= 80%): mfe1 was fully excluded\n  from ci-verify.yml''s test filter to work around one pre-existing broken\n  test (tests/index.test.tsx — a real, un-mocked Apollo Client network\n  call whose outcome depends on a live router being reachable, unrelated\n  to any US-16 work). That excluded RegisterPage.tsx''s real coverage\n  (from the passing tests/integration/register.test.tsx) from ever\n  reaching Sonar too. Fix: exclude just the one broken file at the\n  rstest.config.ts level (documented there) instead of the whole package,\n  re-include mfe1 in CI''s filter, and wire up its own istanbul-lcov\n  coverage the same way packages/server/script and servers/auth already\n  were. RegisterPage.tsx now reports 97.14% line coverage.\n  Also reformats mfe1''s own pre-existing biome debt (8 files) — needed\n  now that it''s back in the format-check step for the first time.\n\n- B Security Rating on New Code (required >= A): one new OPEN\n  kubernetes:S5332 (clear-text protocol) finding on\n  services/apollo/helm/values.yaml:23 (the auth.url subgraph entry added\n  in FEAT-02) — same already-accepted internal-cluster-only pattern as\n  the test1.url/test2.url entries in the same file.\n\n* fix(apollo): give the rover compose test enough time for a cold plugin download (#37)\n\nFixes #36 — bun:test''s default 5000ms timeout wasn''t enough: rover\ndownloads its ''supergraph'' compose plugin on first use in a fresh\nenvironment (confirmed in CI, https://github.com/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/actions/runs/29221424669).\nNever caught locally, since rover isn''t installed there and the test just\nskips. 30s covers a cold download; a warm rover finishes in well under a\nsecond either way.\n\n* fix(authentik): healthcheck used wget, which the image doesn''t ship (#43)\n\nauthentik-server''s healthcheck (\"wget --no-verbose --spider ...\") always\nexited 127 (wget not found — confirmed via `docker exec authentik-server\nwhich wget`), leaving the container permanently \"unhealthy\" regardless of\nwhether authentik itself was actually serving traffic. This blocks\nservers/auth''s `depends_on: condition: service_healthy`, so `docker\ncompose up auth` never started.\n\ncurl is present in the image; swapped to that. Verified: authentik-server\nnow reports healthy within its 30s start_period, and `docker compose up\n-d auth` (which depends on it) starts and serves GraphQL immediately.\n\nPre-existing bug (services/authentik/docker-compose.yml, introduced in\n6ea0c18, unrelated to #16) — found while setting up a local end-to-end\nmanual test of the register flow.\n\n* fix(register): resolve Sonar code-quality findings from FEAT-01/04 (#39)\n\nPR #33''s SonarCloud quality gate flagged 8 code smells on new code:\n- Two super-linear (ReDoS-prone) email regexes (RegisterPage.tsx,\n  RegisterUseCase.ts) — domain labels now exclude ''.'', removing the\n  backtracking ambiguity between the two adjacent [^\\s@]+ groups.\n- Deprecated `FormEvent` (React 19 removed it in favor of the concrete\n  event type) — switched to `SubmitEvent`.\n- Deprecated `useMutation<TData, TVariables>(...)` generic-args overload —\n  typed `REGISTER_MUTATION` itself as a `TypedDocumentNode`, so the hook\n  infers instead.\n- Ambiguous JSX whitespace between label text and the next input — wrapped\n  label text in an explicit `<span>`.\n- `role=\"status\"` on a `<p>` — swapped for the native `<output>` element.\n\nVerified: mfe1 + auth tests still pass, mfe1 typecheck clean, no\nunrelated files touched.\n\n* fix(mfe1): wire RegisterPage to the /register route (#41)\n\nFEAT-04 (#20) scaffolded RegisterPage + its viewmodel/types but never\nadded it to router.tsx''s route tree — the spec calls for \"React Router\nroute /register\" explicitly, and there was no way to reach the page in\na running app (only via its own test file, which renders it directly).\n\nAlso splits the previously single catch-all rootRoute (which always\nrendered Test1Page) into an index route (\"/\") + the new /register\nroute, both under a shared root that now just renders <Outlet />.\n\n* fix(register): move mutation+error handling out of the component body (#45)\n\nReproduced at runtime: submitting the register form threw\n\"ReferenceError: error is not defined\" from inside handleSubmit. Root\ncause is Rsbuild''s React Compiler plugin (reactCompiler: true) — the\ncompiled output referenced the `catch` clause''s bound variable outside\nthe scope it generated a declaration for. RegisterPage was the first\ncomponent in this app with a try/catch in an event handler, so nothing\nelse had hit this before.\n\nFix: extract the mutation call + try/catch into submitRegistration, a\nplain top-level function outside the component. React Compiler only\ntransforms functions matching its Component/Hook naming heuristic, so\nthis sidesteps the bug rather than working around its internals.\n\nVerified: manually reproduced and confirmed fixed against the local\ndocker-compose stack (auth + authentik + apollo router), mfe1 tests\nstill pass, typecheck clean.\n\n* fix(terraform): wire auth''s terraform module into the root aggregator (#47)\n\nservers/auth/terraform/module was fully built (FEAT-02/03 k8s work —\nnamespace, helm_release, Authentik secret wiring) but never added to\nterraform/main.tf''s module blocks, unlike test1/test2/mfe1/web1. A\n`terraform apply` at the root never touched auth at all — same class\nof gap as #40 (RegisterPage scaffolded but never routed).\n\nAdds module \"auth\" (mirroring mfe1''s shape — namespace + app_image_tag\nonly, no kafka/schema-registry inputs since auth has neither), plus the\nmatching auth_namespace/auth_app_image_tag variables and\nauth_namespace/auth_release_status outputs.\n\nVerified: `terraform validate` passes. Not applied against the real\n(S3-backed) root state as part of this fix — that''s a separate,\nexplicit deploy step.\n\n* fix(terraform): wire authentik''s bootstrap.token through to k8s (#49)\n\nservices/authentik/helm/values.yaml''s bootstrap.token defaulted to \"\"\nwith no way to set it via the services/terraform root — unlike\nsecretKey/postgresql.password/bootstrap.password, it had no\ncorresponding Terraform variable. Without a real token, an in-cluster\nAuthentik has no way for servers/auth/ansible''s provisioning role to\nauthenticate against it at all (AUTHENTIK_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN-based auth,\nsee services/authentik/CLAUDE.md).\n\nAdds bootstrap_token to services/authentik/terraform/module (default\n\"\", sensitive) and threads it through services/terraform''s own\nauthentik_bootstrap_token variable, mirroring the existing\nsecret_key/postgresql_password/bootstrap_password pattern exactly.\n\nVerified: `terraform validate` passes for both services/terraform and\nservices/authentik/terraform.\n\n* fix(auth): let AUTHENTIK_URL override vars.yml''s hardcoded target (#51)\n\nservers/auth/ansible/vars.yml hardcoded authentik_url to the\ndocker-compose service hostname (http://authentik-server:9000), only\nreachable from the \"authentik-ansible\" tool container''s own network.\nThere was no way to point the provisioning role at a different\nAuthentik instance (e.g. an in-cluster one reached via `kubectl\nport-forward`) without editing the committed file.\n\nSame lookup(''env'', ...) | default(...) convention already used two\nlines down for authentik_bootstrap_token. Verified with a throwaway\nplaybook: no AUTHENTIK_URL set resolves to the unchanged\ndocker-compose default; AUTHENTIK_URL=http://localhost:9001 resolves\nto the override.\n\nIn-cluster usage: run `ansible-playbook` directly (already installed\nlocally — no docker compose needed) rather than through `bun run\nauth:provision`''s docker-compose wrapper, which has no network route\nto a k8s Service.\n\n* fix(apollo): supergraph.graphql''s k8s copy was missing the mutation root type (#53)\n\nservices/apollo/helm/files/supergraph.graphql''s schema block only\ndeclared `query: Query` — no `mutation: Mutation`, even though\n`type Mutation @join__type(graph: AUTH) { ... }` was present further\ndown in the same file. Apollo Router rejected every mutation with\n\"The schema has no ''mutation'' root type defined\", confirmed against a\nlive in-cluster router.\n\nservices/apollo/dist/supergraph.graphql (the docker-compose-generated\nversion) has always had `mutation: Mutation` correctly — this file is\na hand-maintained copy (see services/apollo/CLAUDE.md''s \"Kubernetes\ndeployment uses a hand-patched copy\" section) and the line was dropped\nat some point during a manual edit, unnoticed since nothing exercised\na k8s-deployed mutation until now.\n\nVerified end-to-end against a real in-cluster Apollo Router: the\n`register` mutation now returns {\"success\":true,\"message\":\n\"Registration successful.\"} through the router, reaching the in-cluster\nauth subgraph and Authentik.\n\n* fix(terraform): raise helm_release timeout across every module (#55)\n\nEvery helm_release resource in this repo (5 app modules + 9 service\nmodules) relied on the provider default (300s). Hit repeatedly during\nUS-16''s k8s verification: \"context deadline exceeded\" on module.auth\nand module.test1 mid-apply — auth needed real Authentik credentials\nthat don''t exist until after the release lands (a separate chicken/egg,\nnot fixed here), and test1''s own crashloop meant neither reached\nReady before the default timeout. Bumped to 600s everywhere, uniformly\n— all 14 modules share the exact same resource shape from the same\nturbo gen template, so the same gap exists in all of them.\n\nVerified: `terraform fmt -recursive` + `terraform validate` clean for\nboth terraform/ and services/terraform.\n\n* fix: :bug: Force building terraform with s3\n\n* fix(ci): regenerate bun.lock after e2e was dropped from workspaces\n\nPR #33''s CI failed on `bun install --frozen-lockfile`: \"lockfile had\nchanges, but lockfile is frozen\". 2ba6f8c removed \"e2e\" from the root\npackage.json''s workspaces array but never regenerated bun.lock to\nmatch, so the lockfile still referenced the e2e workspace and its\ndeps (cypress, vitest, etc.) — a frozen install correctly refused to\nproceed with a stale lockfile.\n\nAlso untracks servers/auth/.turbo/turbo-test.log (a build artifact\ncommitted by the same commit) and closes the gap that let it happen:\n.gitignore''s `/.turbo` only matched the repo root, not nested\n`.turbo` dirs — added `/**/*/.turbo`, matching every other ignored\nbuild-output pattern in this file (node_modules, .env, coverage,\n.terraform all already have both variants).\n\nVerified: `bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts` (CI''s exact\ncommand) now succeeds locally.\n\n* chore(run-state): US-01 feature PRs merged, FEAT-05/#22 login mutation PR opened\n\nConfirmed PRs #27/#28/#29/#30/#31 merged. Also flags that\nrelease/integration-testing has advanced beyond this file''s prior\nsnapshot (US-16 appears fully merged in) via external developer\nactivity outside this run''s own /run continue tracking.\n\n* [US-02] User Sign In (#58)\n\n* test(e2e): add e2e tests for User Sign In\n\n* [FEAT-22] Login Mutation (#56)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Login Mutation\n\n* feat(auth): add login mutation, replacing signIn\n\nAdds a login(email, password): AuthPayload! GraphQL mutation on\nservers/auth, replacing signIn. Reuses AuthentikClient.signIn()''s\nexisting Flow Executor + Authorization Code sign-in, mapping email to\nAuthentik''s username field. Wrong password and non-existent email\nreturn the identical INVALID_CREDENTIALS error (anti-enumeration), and\na malformed Authentik token response is rejected server-side rather\nthan partially leaking through to the client.\n\nCloses #22\n\n* chore(api): regenerate auth GraphQL types for login mutation\n\nRegenerated via servers/auth''s bun run gen after replacing signIn\nwith login in its GraphQL schema.\n\n* [FEAT-23] Sign In UI and Token Storage (#57)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Sign In UI and Token Storage\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(mfe1): add sign-in UI and token storage\n\nAdds a LoginPage at /login, mirroring RegisterPage''s module shape\n(pages/types/viewmodel). On submit, calls the login mutation via\nApollo Router; on success writes the full token set to localStorage\n(auth_access_token/auth_refresh_token/auth_id_token) and shows a\nsuccess message; on mutation failure or unreachable network shows an\nerror message; on a localStorage write failure shows a separate\nstorage error, distinct from the mutation error region.\n\nAuthPayload/login aren''t in packages/api''s generated auth types on\nthis branch yet (FEAT-05/#22 hasn''t merged into us/21-user-sign-in),\nso the payload shape is declared locally against the fixed SDL\ncontract in auth.api.graphql instead of imported from AuthGraphql.\n\nAlso fixes tests/rstest.setup.ts: Bun 1.3.14 defines its own inert\nglobalThis.localStorage, which shadows happy-dom''s real\nimplementation in rstest''s environment setup (installGlobal only\noverrides keys not already present in global) and left\nwindow.localStorage.getItem/setItem throwing on undefined. Added a\nminimal Storage polyfill in setup so any test touching localStorage\nworks, plus an afterEach clear for isolation between tests.\n\nCloses #23\n\n* refactor(mfe1): extract shared CredentialsForm and validation\n\nLoginPage duplicated RegisterPage''s validate() (25 lines) and form\nJSX (50 lines) almost verbatim, tripping SonarCloud''s new-code\nduplication gate (12.9% vs a 3% threshold) on PR #57. Extracted the\nshared email/password validation into lib/credentialsValidation.ts\nand the shared form markup into components/CredentialsForm.tsx, used\nby both RegisterPage and LoginPage — each page now only owns its own\nsubmit handler and post-submit behavior (storage write for login,\nsuccess message for register).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [US-03] User Sign Out (#61)\n\n* test(e2e): add e2e tests for User Sign Out\n\n* [FEAT-07] Logout Mutation (#59)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Logout Mutation\n\n* feat(auth): add logout mutation, replacing signOut\n\nAdds AuthentikClient.logout() (introspect + revoke + best-effort\nsession termination) and LogoutUseCase, wired in place of the old\nsignOut(refreshToken) mutation per FEAT-07''s spec.\n\n* chore(auth): fix biome formatting on generated types and tests\n\nCI''s verify job runs `biome check --write` and fails if that leaves\nan uncommitted diff — these files weren''t formatted to match before\nthe first commit.\n\n* [FEAT-08] Sign Out UI (#60)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Sign Out UI\n\n* feat(mfe1): add Sign Out UI, targeting logout(accessToken)\n\nAdds LogoutPage at /logout: reads auth_access_token, calls the\nlogout mutation, clears all auth_* localStorage keys regardless of\noutcome, and shows a distinct message for success/error/network\nerror/not-signed-in.\n\ntest(mfe1): update logout.test.tsx to logout(accessToken):LogoutPayload\n\nThe pre-existing test pinned the old signOut(refreshToken):Boolean!\ncontract, written before FEAT-07 replaced it. Both issues #25/#26 and\nthe OpenSpec SDL agree on logout(accessToken) — updated per developer\nconfirmation.\n\nchore(mfe1): polyfill localStorage in rstest setup\n\nrstest''s DOM environment provides window/document but not\nlocalStorage — logout is the first module here to touch it in a\ntest.\n\n* test(mfe1): cover the success:false branch and router wiring\n\nAdds the missing LogoutPage case where the mutation resolves without\nerrors but the payload itself reports failure, and a router.tsx test\nso the new /logout route registration isn''t 0%-covered \"new code\".\n\nchore: exclude test-setup files from Sonar coverage\n\nfrontends/*/tests/**/*.setup.ts is test infrastructure, not\napplication code, and isn''t in rstest''s own lcov output — same\nrationale as the existing packages/script/src/release exclusion.\n\n* fix(k8s): e2e workspace breaks web1/mfe1 Docker builds (#62)\n\n* fix(k8s): add e2e workspace''s package.json to web1/mfe1 Docker builds\n\nRoot package.json''s `workspaces` now lists \"e2e\" as a literal path\n(not a glob like \"apps/*\"/\"packages/*\"), added to trigger e2e test\nruns. web1/mfe1''s Dockerfiles COPY only a partial subset of the repo\nbefore `bun install`; a glob matching nothing is tolerated, but a\nliteral path must exist or bun hard-fails with \"Workspace not found\ne2e\". auth/test1/test2 are unaffected since their Dockerfiles use\n`turbo prune --docker`, which already trims `workspaces` to the kept\nsubset.\n\n* chore: :sparkles: Sonarqube skill + regenerated supergraph\n\n* fix(e2e): e2e test:all fails — stale branch + wrong host defaults (#63)\n\n* [US-02] User Sign In (#58)\n\n* test(e2e): add e2e tests for User Sign In\n\n* [FEAT-22] Login Mutation (#56)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Login Mutation\n\n* feat(auth): add login mutation, replacing signIn\n\nAdds a login(email, password): AuthPayload! GraphQL mutation on\nservers/auth, replacing signIn. Reuses AuthentikClient.signIn()''s\nexisting Flow Executor + Authorization Code sign-in, mapping email to\nAuthentik''s username field. Wrong password and non-existent email\nreturn the identical INVALID_CREDENTIALS error (anti-enumeration), and\na malformed Authentik token response is rejected server-side rather\nthan partially leaking through to the client.\n\nCloses #22\n\n* chore(api): regenerate auth GraphQL types for login mutation\n\nRegenerated via servers/auth''s bun run gen after replacing signIn\nwith login in its GraphQL schema.\n\n* [FEAT-23] Sign In UI and Token Storage (#57)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Sign In UI and Token Storage\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(mfe1): add sign-in UI and token storage\n\nAdds a LoginPage at /login, mirroring RegisterPage''s module shape\n(pages/types/viewmodel). On submit, calls the login mutation via\nApollo Router; on success writes the full token set to localStorage\n(auth_access_token/auth_refresh_token/auth_id_token) and shows a\nsuccess message; on mutation failure or unreachable network shows an\nerror message; on a localStorage write failure shows a separate\nstorage error, distinct from the mutation error region.\n\nAuthPayload/login aren''t in packages/api''s generated auth types on\nthis branch yet (FEAT-05/#22 hasn''t merged into us/21-user-sign-in),\nso the payload shape is declared locally against the fixed SDL\ncontract in auth.api.graphql instead of imported from AuthGraphql.\n\nAlso fixes tests/rstest.setup.ts: Bun 1.3.14 defines its own inert\nglobalThis.localStorage, which shadows happy-dom''s real\nimplementation in rstest''s environment setup (installGlobal only\noverrides keys not already present in global) and left\nwindow.localStorage.getItem/setItem throwing on undefined. Added a\nminimal Storage polyfill in setup so any test touching localStorage\nworks, plus an afterEach clear for isolation between tests.\n\nCloses #23\n\n* refactor(mfe1): extract shared CredentialsForm and validation\n\nLoginPage duplicated RegisterPage''s validate() (25 lines) and form\nJSX (50 lines) almost verbatim, tripping SonarCloud''s new-code\nduplication gate (12.9% vs a 3% threshold) on PR #57. Extracted the\nshared email/password validation into lib/credentialsValidation.ts\nand the shared form markup into components/CredentialsForm.tsx, used\nby both RegisterPage and LoginPage — each page now only owns its own\nsubmit handler and post-submit behavior (storage write for login,\nsuccess message for register).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): target graphql.localhost/mfe1.localhost, not bare localhost\n\nEvery browser-facing service in this repo is routed through Traefik\non a distinct *.localhost Host (see services/traefik/CLAUDE.md) —\nthere is no bare-localhost route for either Apollo Router or mfe1, so\nCLUSTER_URL''s shared default couldn''t serve both \"call the GraphQL\nAPI\" and \"visit a page\". Split into GRAPHQL_URL (default\nhttp://graphql.localhost) and FRONTEND_URL (default\nhttp://mfe1.localhost), and fixed logout.cy.ts''s setup calls to hit\nGRAPHQL_URL instead of Cypress.config().baseUrl.\n\nVerified end-to-end against a live docker-compose stack (authentik +\nauth server + Apollo Router): register -> login -> logout all pass\nthrough the router, and e2e/test:api (11/11) passes.\n\n* fix(e2e): default to direct service ports, not *.localhost\n\nNode''s own dns.lookup (which Vitest''s api/**/*.test.ts suite runs\nunder, unlike Cypress''s browser-based network stack) does not\nresolve arbitrary *.localhost subdomains per RFC 6761 the way\nbrowsers/curl/Bun do — confirmed empirically: only the exact string\n\"localhost\" is special-cased; \"graphql.localhost\" throws ENOTFOUND.\nThe previous commit''s *.localhost defaults were correct per Traefik''s\nown routing convention but unusable under plain Node.\n\nDefault to each service''s own direct host-port publish instead\n(services/apollo/docker-compose.yml''s 4000:4000, frontends/mfe1''s\n3001:3001) — every routed service keeps this alongside its Traefik\nroute (services/traefik/CLAUDE.md), so this sidesteps the DNS gap\nwithout losing any routing behavior, and doesn''t depend on Traefik\nbeing reachable at all for local e2e runs.\n\nVerified: e2e/test:api now passes (11/11) with zero env var\noverrides, against the same live docker-compose stack from the\nprevious commit.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): resolve release-manifest against origin/main, not local main\n\nactions/checkout with fetch-depth: 0 only populates origin/main as a\nremote-tracking ref when checking out a release/hotfix branch — the\nbare local branch main is never created, so git diff main...HEAD\nfailed with exit 128 in touchedApps().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): add missing version field to server package.json files\n\nrelease:cut reads each touched deployable app''s package.json \"version\"\nto seed its release entry — none of servers/{auth,test1,test2} had one,\nso the very first cut for this release branch failed on the first\ntouched server. frontends/*, apps/*, and root package.json already\ncarry version: \"1.0.0\"; servers were the only gap.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): grant contents:write to jobs that push commits back\n\ngithub-actions[bot] got a 403 pushing the release-manifest commit —\nthis repo''s default GITHUB_TOKEN permissions are read-only, and none\nof these three jobs (release-manifest, promote, hotfix) declared an\nexplicit permissions block, so they never had write access to begin\nwith. Scoped to just these jobs rather than flipping the repo-wide\ndefault, since none of their other steps need any broader scope.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(release): update release manifest [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e32058dbb931088bb422c165c043a6b32a6c285e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/git/trees/e32058dbb931088bb422c165c043a6b32a6c285e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/git/commits/59390458243eb0bb941dd9b5ba902cca579d71ce","verification":{"payload":"tree e32058dbb931088bb422c165c043a6b32a6c285e\nparent f1039cb82cbb34ce6a11a1d75279d6e5e27763ef\nauthor Edward Lim Kok Siong <edwardlimkoksiong1994@gmail.com> 1784022187 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784022187 +0800\n\nRelease: integration-testing (US-01/02/03 — Registration, Sign In, Sign Out) (#64)\n\n* feat: :sparkles: Claude Code config\n\n* chore(openspec): add requirements for integration-testing\n\n* chore(openspec): fix requirements for integration-testing\n\nRetarget FEAT-01/05/07 at the existing ./servers/auth service instead of\nscaffolding a new auth-subgraph (servers/auth already implements\nsignIn/signUp/signOut against authentik). Also fixes Phase 0 validation\ngaps: missing null placeholders on backend features, PENDING Claude\nDesign URL markers on FEAT-04/06/08 (no design handoff this release,\nper prior developer decision), and missing e2e labels on all three user\nstories.\n\n* chore(run-state): pm phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to qa\n\n* chore(e2e): scaffold e2e project with vitest and cypress\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* [US-16] User Registration (#33)\n\n* test(e2e): add e2e tests for User Registration\n\n* [FEAT-19] Authentik Terraform and Helm Configuration (#28)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Authentik Terraform and Helm Configuration\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* feat(auth): wire Authentik credentials into servers/auth''s Helm chart\n\nAdds authentik-secret.yaml (mirrors servers/test1''s vault-secret.yaml\npattern — manually-filled placeholders, since there''s no in-cluster\nequivalent of auth:provision yet) and AUTHENTIK_URL to the ConfigMap,\nwired into the Deployment via envFrom. Previously servers/auth''s Helm\nchart had no Authentik wiring at all.\n\nAlso corrects the QA-written FEAT-03 integration test: it checked for a\ndedicated Authentik enrollment Flow, but FEAT-01''s register() mutation\nended up using the existing Admin API (AuthentikClient.enroll(), a thin\nwrapper over createUser()) rather than driving a Flow Executor\nenrollment flow. Replaced with a check that the service account is\nactually authorized to create users, which is what register() really\ndepends on — verified passing against the live local Authentik instance.\n\nCloses #19\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* [FEAT-18] Apollo Router Subgraph Wiring (#29)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Apollo Router Subgraph Wiring\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* feat(apollo): join servers/auth to the graphql network, wire it into the composed supergraph\n\nservers/auth was already listed in services/apollo/src/config/supergraph.yaml\nbut unreachable — it was only on the authentik docker network, not the\ngraphql network apollo-router and the other subgraphs share. Verified fixed\nagainst the live local stack: register/signIn/signOut all now reach the auth\nsubgraph through the router (previously schema-validation errors, since the\ncomposed schema never had AUTH in it either).\n\nAlso hand-patches services/apollo/helm/files/supergraph.graphql (the\nk8s-deployed composed schema — hand-maintained, not auto-generated; see\nservices/apollo/CLAUDE.md) with the same AUTH subgraph wiring, and adds\nservices/apollo/helm/values.yaml''s auth.url. rover CLI wasn''t available in\nthis environment to verify via bun run supergraph — reasoned through from\nthe already-correct docker-compose composition and the identical TEST1/TEST2\npattern.\n\nAlso corrects the QA-written integration test, which targeted the auth\nsubgraph''s old signUp mutation before FEAT-01 (#17) renamed it to register.\n\nCloses #18\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* fix(apollo): skip live router tests gracefully when unreachable\n\nSame gap the authentik integration test already had fixed: 3 of these\ntests require a real running Apollo Router + auth subgraph\n(docker-compose), which CI doesn''t have — they were failing with\nConnectionRefused instead of skipping. Adds the same top-level\nreachability probe + test.skipIf(!routerReachable) pattern as\nservices/authentik/tests/integration/enrollment-and-auth-flows.test.ts.\nVerified both ways: 4 pass/1 skip against the live local stack, 1 pass/4\nskip (0 fail) with an unreachable router URL.\n\n* [FEAT-17] Auth Register Mutation (#27)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Auth Register Mutation\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* feat(auth): add register mutation, replacing signUp\n\nAdds a register(email, password): RegisterPayload GraphQL mutation on\nservers/auth, replacing signUp. Uses AuthentikClient.enroll() — a thin\nwrapper over the existing Admin API createUser() using the email as\nAuthentik''s username, so duplicate-email registrations surface as the\nsame username-uniqueness violation createUser() callers already detect.\n\nCloses #17\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* [FEAT-20] Register UI (#31)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Register UI\n\n* chore(run-state): qa phase complete for integration-testing, handing off to dev\n\n* feat(mfe1): add Register UI\n\nAdds a /register page (RegisterPage, wired into the register module''s\npages/types/viewmodel structure, mirroring modules/test1) with email/\npassword fields, inline validation, a loading state on submit, and a\nsingle error region covering both GraphQL and network failures — no\nClaude Design handoff this release (developer decision, matching FEAT-01''s\nregister mutation this calls via Apollo Router).\n\nAlso wires up React Testing Library''s cleanup() in rstest.setup.ts (afterEach)\n— not configured by default under rstest, so every test''s rendered DOM was\naccumulating in the same document. Harmless for existing single-test files,\nbut broke this feature''s 6-test suite outright.\n\nCloses #20\n\n* chore(run-state): all US-01 feature PRs open, plus a CI infra fix PR\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail (#30)\n\n* fix(ci): fix bun install ordering so servers/test1''s postinstall doesn''t always fail\n\nservers/test1''s postinstall (prisma generate) loads prisma.config.ts, which\nimports createPrismaConfig from the script workspace package — but script is\nonly source at bun-install time (built separately via turbo run build), and\nits package.json exports field has no unbuilt-source fallback. A single\nbun install --frozen-lockfile has therefore always failed here: confirmed\nagainst every CI run in this repo''s history, including the very first PR\nand the abandoned prior attempt at this release''s US-01.\n\nFix: install with --ignore-scripts, build script explicitly, then run the\none deferred postinstall. Verified locally end-to-end from a clean\nnode_modules/dist state.\n\n* fix(ci): set a placeholder DATABASE_URL for the deferred postinstall step\n\nFixed one pre-existing gap (bun install postinstall ordering) and immediately\nhit another: Prisma 7''s config loader validates DATABASE_URL is resolvable\nbefore generate can even run, and CI has never set it. prisma generate never\nactually connects, so any syntactically-valid connection string satisfies\nthis — verified locally against an unreachable host.\n\n* fix(ci): set sonar.organization\n\nCI on PR #30 failed the SonarQube scan step with ''You must define the\nfollowing mandatory properties: sonar.organization''. Confirmed the correct\nvalue (edwardlim1994) via SonarCloud''s own component API.\n\n* chore: :alembic: Debug SONAR_TOKEN\n\n* chore:\n\n* fix: :bug: Use hash for Sonar scan instead of version number\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build (#32)\n\n* fix(turbo): make test task depend on ^build\n\nCI failed on PR #27: server/package.json''s exports field points only at\ndist/index.js, which doesn''t exist until packages/server is built. dev/\ncompile tasks already declare dependsOn: [\"^build\"]; test never did, so\nturbo ran auth#test before server#build. Verified locally end-to-end: with\nthis fix, turbo run test --filter=auth builds api/script/server first,\nthen auth''s own 11 tests pass.\n\n* fix(script): correct APIGenerator test premise for graphql-codegen\n\n''generate() skips graphql-codegen and protoc when neither binary is\ninstalled'' assumed neither was present — but graphql-codegen is a real\ndevDependency of packages/script itself, so checkDependency(''graphql-codegen'')\nis always true here. That took the ''installed'' branch, which calls Bun.$\n(unavailable under rstest''s Node runtime), throwing and aborting generate()\nbefore the protoc check is ever reached. Never caught before because CI never\ngot this far (masked by the postinstall-ordering bug, then the missing\ntest.dependsOn fix in this same PR). Split into two tests that match what''s\nactually observable: no graphql-codegen warning, and an error log from the\nBun.$ failure instead of an unreachable protoc warning.\n\n* fix(ci): exclude mfe1/web1 from the affected-package check/test step\n\nBoth have pre-existing, unrelated test failures (mfe1: happy-dom fetch-abort;\nweb1: needs a Module Federation runtime rstest doesn''t bootstrap) — not fixed\nby this PR. turbo.json being root config sweeps every package into the\naffected set on any change to it, including these two, so they''d otherwise\nblock CI on unrelated pre-existing bugs.\n\n* fix(ci): wire up real coverage reporting, then reformat repo-wide\n\nRoot cause of the earlier Sonar coverage-gate collision (0% on any\nnewly-touched line): no coverage report existed anywhere in this pipeline,\nso any reformatted line always read as uncovered new code regardless of\nreal test coverage.\n\n- Enables istanbul-lcov coverage in packages/server, packages/script, and\n  servers/auth''s rstest configs (all already had unwired @rstest/core;\n  servers/auth had no rstest.config.ts at all).\n- Adds packages/server/tests/plugin/AuthentikPlugin.test.ts — this file\n  had zero coverage (no test file existed for it, pre-existing gap, not\n  introduced by FEAT-01). Covers AuthentikClient''s HTTP-calling methods\n  via a manual global-fetch stand-in (no injection point exists, same\n  ''manual test double, no module mocking'' convention as this repo''s other\n  tests) plus AuthentikPlugin''s own onStart/onStop wiring. 90.58% line\n  coverage, up from 0%.\n- sonar-project.properties: points sonar.javascript.lcov.reportPaths at\n  the three packages'' coverage output; excludes\n  packages/script/src/release/** (release-automation tooling, genuinely\n  untested pre-existing debt, same precedent as the already-excluded\n  generated API code — not part of any server''s runtime path this release\n  touches).\n- .gitignore: coverage/ output directories.\n- Reformats the same 44 pre-existing files biome --write always wanted\n  fixed (verified all tests still pass, coverage numbers unaffected).\n\nVerified locally: all of server/script/auth/apollo/authentik''s test\nsuites pass; AuthentikPlugin.ts/VaultPgAdapter.ts (the files Sonar\noriginally flagged) both now show real, non-zero coverage.\n\n* fix(ci): restore mfe1 coverage to Sonar, accept the new clear-text finding (#35)\n\nFixes #34 — PR #33''s Quality Gate failed on two conditions:\n\n- 59.0% Coverage on New Code (required >= 80%): mfe1 was fully excluded\n  from ci-verify.yml''s test filter to work around one pre-existing broken\n  test (tests/index.test.tsx — a real, un-mocked Apollo Client network\n  call whose outcome depends on a live router being reachable, unrelated\n  to any US-16 work). That excluded RegisterPage.tsx''s real coverage\n  (from the passing tests/integration/register.test.tsx) from ever\n  reaching Sonar too. Fix: exclude just the one broken file at the\n  rstest.config.ts level (documented there) instead of the whole package,\n  re-include mfe1 in CI''s filter, and wire up its own istanbul-lcov\n  coverage the same way packages/server/script and servers/auth already\n  were. RegisterPage.tsx now reports 97.14% line coverage.\n  Also reformats mfe1''s own pre-existing biome debt (8 files) — needed\n  now that it''s back in the format-check step for the first time.\n\n- B Security Rating on New Code (required >= A): one new OPEN\n  kubernetes:S5332 (clear-text protocol) finding on\n  services/apollo/helm/values.yaml:23 (the auth.url subgraph entry added\n  in FEAT-02) — same already-accepted internal-cluster-only pattern as\n  the test1.url/test2.url entries in the same file.\n\n* fix(apollo): give the rover compose test enough time for a cold plugin download (#37)\n\nFixes #36 — bun:test''s default 5000ms timeout wasn''t enough: rover\ndownloads its ''supergraph'' compose plugin on first use in a fresh\nenvironment (confirmed in CI, https://github.com/EdwardLim1994/microservice-rnd1/actions/runs/29221424669).\nNever caught locally, since rover isn''t installed there and the test just\nskips. 30s covers a cold download; a warm rover finishes in well under a\nsecond either way.\n\n* fix(authentik): healthcheck used wget, which the image doesn''t ship (#43)\n\nauthentik-server''s healthcheck (\"wget --no-verbose --spider ...\") always\nexited 127 (wget not found — confirmed via `docker exec authentik-server\nwhich wget`), leaving the container permanently \"unhealthy\" regardless of\nwhether authentik itself was actually serving traffic. This blocks\nservers/auth''s `depends_on: condition: service_healthy`, so `docker\ncompose up auth` never started.\n\ncurl is present in the image; swapped to that. Verified: authentik-server\nnow reports healthy within its 30s start_period, and `docker compose up\n-d auth` (which depends on it) starts and serves GraphQL immediately.\n\nPre-existing bug (services/authentik/docker-compose.yml, introduced in\n6ea0c18, unrelated to #16) — found while setting up a local end-to-end\nmanual test of the register flow.\n\n* fix(register): resolve Sonar code-quality findings from FEAT-01/04 (#39)\n\nPR #33''s SonarCloud quality gate flagged 8 code smells on new code:\n- Two super-linear (ReDoS-prone) email regexes (RegisterPage.tsx,\n  RegisterUseCase.ts) — domain labels now exclude ''.'', removing the\n  backtracking ambiguity between the two adjacent [^\\s@]+ groups.\n- Deprecated `FormEvent` (React 19 removed it in favor of the concrete\n  event type) — switched to `SubmitEvent`.\n- Deprecated `useMutation<TData, TVariables>(...)` generic-args overload —\n  typed `REGISTER_MUTATION` itself as a `TypedDocumentNode`, so the hook\n  infers instead.\n- Ambiguous JSX whitespace between label text and the next input — wrapped\n  label text in an explicit `<span>`.\n- `role=\"status\"` on a `<p>` — swapped for the native `<output>` element.\n\nVerified: mfe1 + auth tests still pass, mfe1 typecheck clean, no\nunrelated files touched.\n\n* fix(mfe1): wire RegisterPage to the /register route (#41)\n\nFEAT-04 (#20) scaffolded RegisterPage + its viewmodel/types but never\nadded it to router.tsx''s route tree — the spec calls for \"React Router\nroute /register\" explicitly, and there was no way to reach the page in\na running app (only via its own test file, which renders it directly).\n\nAlso splits the previously single catch-all rootRoute (which always\nrendered Test1Page) into an index route (\"/\") + the new /register\nroute, both under a shared root that now just renders <Outlet />.\n\n* fix(register): move mutation+error handling out of the component body (#45)\n\nReproduced at runtime: submitting the register form threw\n\"ReferenceError: error is not defined\" from inside handleSubmit. Root\ncause is Rsbuild''s React Compiler plugin (reactCompiler: true) — the\ncompiled output referenced the `catch` clause''s bound variable outside\nthe scope it generated a declaration for. RegisterPage was the first\ncomponent in this app with a try/catch in an event handler, so nothing\nelse had hit this before.\n\nFix: extract the mutation call + try/catch into submitRegistration, a\nplain top-level function outside the component. React Compiler only\ntransforms functions matching its Component/Hook naming heuristic, so\nthis sidesteps the bug rather than working around its internals.\n\nVerified: manually reproduced and confirmed fixed against the local\ndocker-compose stack (auth + authentik + apollo router), mfe1 tests\nstill pass, typecheck clean.\n\n* fix(terraform): wire auth''s terraform module into the root aggregator (#47)\n\nservers/auth/terraform/module was fully built (FEAT-02/03 k8s work —\nnamespace, helm_release, Authentik secret wiring) but never added to\nterraform/main.tf''s module blocks, unlike test1/test2/mfe1/web1. A\n`terraform apply` at the root never touched auth at all — same class\nof gap as #40 (RegisterPage scaffolded but never routed).\n\nAdds module \"auth\" (mirroring mfe1''s shape — namespace + app_image_tag\nonly, no kafka/schema-registry inputs since auth has neither), plus the\nmatching auth_namespace/auth_app_image_tag variables and\nauth_namespace/auth_release_status outputs.\n\nVerified: `terraform validate` passes. Not applied against the real\n(S3-backed) root state as part of this fix — that''s a separate,\nexplicit deploy step.\n\n* fix(terraform): wire authentik''s bootstrap.token through to k8s (#49)\n\nservices/authentik/helm/values.yaml''s bootstrap.token defaulted to \"\"\nwith no way to set it via the services/terraform root — unlike\nsecretKey/postgresql.password/bootstrap.password, it had no\ncorresponding Terraform variable. Without a real token, an in-cluster\nAuthentik has no way for servers/auth/ansible''s provisioning role to\nauthenticate against it at all (AUTHENTIK_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN-based auth,\nsee services/authentik/CLAUDE.md).\n\nAdds bootstrap_token to services/authentik/terraform/module (default\n\"\", sensitive) and threads it through services/terraform''s own\nauthentik_bootstrap_token variable, mirroring the existing\nsecret_key/postgresql_password/bootstrap_password pattern exactly.\n\nVerified: `terraform validate` passes for both services/terraform and\nservices/authentik/terraform.\n\n* fix(auth): let AUTHENTIK_URL override vars.yml''s hardcoded target (#51)\n\nservers/auth/ansible/vars.yml hardcoded authentik_url to the\ndocker-compose service hostname (http://authentik-server:9000), only\nreachable from the \"authentik-ansible\" tool container''s own network.\nThere was no way to point the provisioning role at a different\nAuthentik instance (e.g. an in-cluster one reached via `kubectl\nport-forward`) without editing the committed file.\n\nSame lookup(''env'', ...) | default(...) convention already used two\nlines down for authentik_bootstrap_token. Verified with a throwaway\nplaybook: no AUTHENTIK_URL set resolves to the unchanged\ndocker-compose default; AUTHENTIK_URL=http://localhost:9001 resolves\nto the override.\n\nIn-cluster usage: run `ansible-playbook` directly (already installed\nlocally — no docker compose needed) rather than through `bun run\nauth:provision`''s docker-compose wrapper, which has no network route\nto a k8s Service.\n\n* fix(apollo): supergraph.graphql''s k8s copy was missing the mutation root type (#53)\n\nservices/apollo/helm/files/supergraph.graphql''s schema block only\ndeclared `query: Query` — no `mutation: Mutation`, even though\n`type Mutation @join__type(graph: AUTH) { ... }` was present further\ndown in the same file. Apollo Router rejected every mutation with\n\"The schema has no ''mutation'' root type defined\", confirmed against a\nlive in-cluster router.\n\nservices/apollo/dist/supergraph.graphql (the docker-compose-generated\nversion) has always had `mutation: Mutation` correctly — this file is\na hand-maintained copy (see services/apollo/CLAUDE.md''s \"Kubernetes\ndeployment uses a hand-patched copy\" section) and the line was dropped\nat some point during a manual edit, unnoticed since nothing exercised\na k8s-deployed mutation until now.\n\nVerified end-to-end against a real in-cluster Apollo Router: the\n`register` mutation now returns {\"success\":true,\"message\":\n\"Registration successful.\"} through the router, reaching the in-cluster\nauth subgraph and Authentik.\n\n* fix(terraform): raise helm_release timeout across every module (#55)\n\nEvery helm_release resource in this repo (5 app modules + 9 service\nmodules) relied on the provider default (300s). Hit repeatedly during\nUS-16''s k8s verification: \"context deadline exceeded\" on module.auth\nand module.test1 mid-apply — auth needed real Authentik credentials\nthat don''t exist until after the release lands (a separate chicken/egg,\nnot fixed here), and test1''s own crashloop meant neither reached\nReady before the default timeout. Bumped to 600s everywhere, uniformly\n— all 14 modules share the exact same resource shape from the same\nturbo gen template, so the same gap exists in all of them.\n\nVerified: `terraform fmt -recursive` + `terraform validate` clean for\nboth terraform/ and services/terraform.\n\n* fix: :bug: Force building terraform with s3\n\n* fix(ci): regenerate bun.lock after e2e was dropped from workspaces\n\nPR #33''s CI failed on `bun install --frozen-lockfile`: \"lockfile had\nchanges, but lockfile is frozen\". 2ba6f8c removed \"e2e\" from the root\npackage.json''s workspaces array but never regenerated bun.lock to\nmatch, so the lockfile still referenced the e2e workspace and its\ndeps (cypress, vitest, etc.) — a frozen install correctly refused to\nproceed with a stale lockfile.\n\nAlso untracks servers/auth/.turbo/turbo-test.log (a build artifact\ncommitted by the same commit) and closes the gap that let it happen:\n.gitignore''s `/.turbo` only matched the repo root, not nested\n`.turbo` dirs — added `/**/*/.turbo`, matching every other ignored\nbuild-output pattern in this file (node_modules, .env, coverage,\n.terraform all already have both variants).\n\nVerified: `bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts` (CI''s exact\ncommand) now succeeds locally.\n\n* chore(run-state): US-01 feature PRs merged, FEAT-05/#22 login mutation PR opened\n\nConfirmed PRs #27/#28/#29/#30/#31 merged. Also flags that\nrelease/integration-testing has advanced beyond this file''s prior\nsnapshot (US-16 appears fully merged in) via external developer\nactivity outside this run''s own /run continue tracking.\n\n* [US-02] User Sign In (#58)\n\n* test(e2e): add e2e tests for User Sign In\n\n* [FEAT-22] Login Mutation (#56)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Login Mutation\n\n* feat(auth): add login mutation, replacing signIn\n\nAdds a login(email, password): AuthPayload! GraphQL mutation on\nservers/auth, replacing signIn. Reuses AuthentikClient.signIn()''s\nexisting Flow Executor + Authorization Code sign-in, mapping email to\nAuthentik''s username field. Wrong password and non-existent email\nreturn the identical INVALID_CREDENTIALS error (anti-enumeration), and\na malformed Authentik token response is rejected server-side rather\nthan partially leaking through to the client.\n\nCloses #22\n\n* chore(api): regenerate auth GraphQL types for login mutation\n\nRegenerated via servers/auth''s bun run gen after replacing signIn\nwith login in its GraphQL schema.\n\n* [FEAT-23] Sign In UI and Token Storage (#57)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Sign In UI and Token Storage\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(mfe1): add sign-in UI and token storage\n\nAdds a LoginPage at /login, mirroring RegisterPage''s module shape\n(pages/types/viewmodel). On submit, calls the login mutation via\nApollo Router; on success writes the full token set to localStorage\n(auth_access_token/auth_refresh_token/auth_id_token) and shows a\nsuccess message; on mutation failure or unreachable network shows an\nerror message; on a localStorage write failure shows a separate\nstorage error, distinct from the mutation error region.\n\nAuthPayload/login aren''t in packages/api''s generated auth types on\nthis branch yet (FEAT-05/#22 hasn''t merged into us/21-user-sign-in),\nso the payload shape is declared locally against the fixed SDL\ncontract in auth.api.graphql instead of imported from AuthGraphql.\n\nAlso fixes tests/rstest.setup.ts: Bun 1.3.14 defines its own inert\nglobalThis.localStorage, which shadows happy-dom''s real\nimplementation in rstest''s environment setup (installGlobal only\noverrides keys not already present in global) and left\nwindow.localStorage.getItem/setItem throwing on undefined. Added a\nminimal Storage polyfill in setup so any test touching localStorage\nworks, plus an afterEach clear for isolation between tests.\n\nCloses #23\n\n* refactor(mfe1): extract shared CredentialsForm and validation\n\nLoginPage duplicated RegisterPage''s validate() (25 lines) and form\nJSX (50 lines) almost verbatim, tripping SonarCloud''s new-code\nduplication gate (12.9% vs a 3% threshold) on PR #57. Extracted the\nshared email/password validation into lib/credentialsValidation.ts\nand the shared form markup into components/CredentialsForm.tsx, used\nby both RegisterPage and LoginPage — each page now only owns its own\nsubmit handler and post-submit behavior (storage write for login,\nsuccess message for register).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [US-03] User Sign Out (#61)\n\n* test(e2e): add e2e tests for User Sign Out\n\n* [FEAT-07] Logout Mutation (#59)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Logout Mutation\n\n* feat(auth): add logout mutation, replacing signOut\n\nAdds AuthentikClient.logout() (introspect + revoke + best-effort\nsession termination) and LogoutUseCase, wired in place of the old\nsignOut(refreshToken) mutation per FEAT-07''s spec.\n\n* chore(auth): fix biome formatting on generated types and tests\n\nCI''s verify job runs `biome check --write` and fails if that leaves\nan uncommitted diff — these files weren''t formatted to match before\nthe first commit.\n\n* [FEAT-08] Sign Out UI (#60)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Sign Out UI\n\n* feat(mfe1): add Sign Out UI, targeting logout(accessToken)\n\nAdds LogoutPage at /logout: reads auth_access_token, calls the\nlogout mutation, clears all auth_* localStorage keys regardless of\noutcome, and shows a distinct message for success/error/network\nerror/not-signed-in.\n\ntest(mfe1): update logout.test.tsx to logout(accessToken):LogoutPayload\n\nThe pre-existing test pinned the old signOut(refreshToken):Boolean!\ncontract, written before FEAT-07 replaced it. Both issues #25/#26 and\nthe OpenSpec SDL agree on logout(accessToken) — updated per developer\nconfirmation.\n\nchore(mfe1): polyfill localStorage in rstest setup\n\nrstest''s DOM environment provides window/document but not\nlocalStorage — logout is the first module here to touch it in a\ntest.\n\n* test(mfe1): cover the success:false branch and router wiring\n\nAdds the missing LogoutPage case where the mutation resolves without\nerrors but the payload itself reports failure, and a router.tsx test\nso the new /logout route registration isn''t 0%-covered \"new code\".\n\nchore: exclude test-setup files from Sonar coverage\n\nfrontends/*/tests/**/*.setup.ts is test infrastructure, not\napplication code, and isn''t in rstest''s own lcov output — same\nrationale as the existing packages/script/src/release exclusion.\n\n* fix(k8s): e2e workspace breaks web1/mfe1 Docker builds (#62)\n\n* fix(k8s): add e2e workspace''s package.json to web1/mfe1 Docker builds\n\nRoot package.json''s `workspaces` now lists \"e2e\" as a literal path\n(not a glob like \"apps/*\"/\"packages/*\"), added to trigger e2e test\nruns. web1/mfe1''s Dockerfiles COPY only a partial subset of the repo\nbefore `bun install`; a glob matching nothing is tolerated, but a\nliteral path must exist or bun hard-fails with \"Workspace not found\ne2e\". auth/test1/test2 are unaffected since their Dockerfiles use\n`turbo prune --docker`, which already trims `workspaces` to the kept\nsubset.\n\n* chore: :sparkles: Sonarqube skill + regenerated supergraph\n\n* fix(e2e): e2e test:all fails — stale branch + wrong host defaults (#63)\n\n* [US-02] User Sign In (#58)\n\n* test(e2e): add e2e tests for User Sign In\n\n* [FEAT-22] Login Mutation (#56)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Login Mutation\n\n* feat(auth): add login mutation, replacing signIn\n\nAdds a login(email, password): AuthPayload! GraphQL mutation on\nservers/auth, replacing signIn. Reuses AuthentikClient.signIn()''s\nexisting Flow Executor + Authorization Code sign-in, mapping email to\nAuthentik''s username field. Wrong password and non-existent email\nreturn the identical INVALID_CREDENTIALS error (anti-enumeration), and\na malformed Authentik token response is rejected server-side rather\nthan partially leaking through to the client.\n\nCloses #22\n\n* chore(api): regenerate auth GraphQL types for login mutation\n\nRegenerated via servers/auth''s bun run gen after replacing signIn\nwith login in its GraphQL schema.\n\n* [FEAT-23] Sign In UI and Token Storage (#57)\n\n* test(integration): add integration tests for Sign In UI and Token Storage\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(mfe1): add sign-in UI and token storage\n\nAdds a LoginPage at /login, mirroring RegisterPage''s module shape\n(pages/types/viewmodel). On submit, calls the login mutation via\nApollo Router; on success writes the full token set to localStorage\n(auth_access_token/auth_refresh_token/auth_id_token) and shows a\nsuccess message; on mutation failure or unreachable network shows an\nerror message; on a localStorage write failure shows a separate\nstorage error, distinct from the mutation error region.\n\nAuthPayload/login aren''t in packages/api''s generated auth types on\nthis branch yet (FEAT-05/#22 hasn''t merged into us/21-user-sign-in),\nso the payload shape is declared locally against the fixed SDL\ncontract in auth.api.graphql instead of imported from AuthGraphql.\n\nAlso fixes tests/rstest.setup.ts: Bun 1.3.14 defines its own inert\nglobalThis.localStorage, which shadows happy-dom''s real\nimplementation in rstest''s environment setup (installGlobal only\noverrides keys not already present in global) and left\nwindow.localStorage.getItem/setItem throwing on undefined. Added a\nminimal Storage polyfill in setup so any test touching localStorage\nworks, plus an afterEach clear for isolation between tests.\n\nCloses #23\n\n* refactor(mfe1): extract shared CredentialsForm and validation\n\nLoginPage duplicated RegisterPage''s validate() (25 lines) and form\nJSX (50 lines) almost verbatim, tripping SonarCloud''s new-code\nduplication gate (12.9% vs a 3% threshold) on PR #57. Extracted the\nshared email/password validation into lib/credentialsValidation.ts\nand the shared form markup into components/CredentialsForm.tsx, used\nby both RegisterPage and LoginPage — each page now only owns its own\nsubmit handler and post-submit behavior (storage write for login,\nsuccess message for register).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(e2e): target graphql.localhost/mfe1.localhost, not bare localhost\n\nEvery browser-facing service in this repo is routed through Traefik\non a distinct *.localhost Host (see services/traefik/CLAUDE.md) —\nthere is no bare-localhost route for either Apollo Router or mfe1, so\nCLUSTER_URL''s shared default couldn''t serve both \"call the GraphQL\nAPI\" and \"visit a page\". Split into GRAPHQL_URL (default\nhttp://graphql.localhost) and FRONTEND_URL (default\nhttp://mfe1.localhost), and fixed logout.cy.ts''s setup calls to hit\nGRAPHQL_URL instead of Cypress.config().baseUrl.\n\nVerified end-to-end against a live docker-compose stack (authentik +\nauth server + Apollo Router): register -> login -> logout all pass\nthrough the router, and e2e/test:api (11/11) passes.\n\n* fix(e2e): default to direct service ports, not *.localhost\n\nNode''s own dns.lookup (which Vitest''s api/**/*.test.ts suite runs\nunder, unlike Cypress''s browser-based network stack) does not\nresolve arbitrary *.localhost subdomains per RFC 6761 the way\nbrowsers/curl/Bun do — confirmed empirically: only the exact string\n\"localhost\" is special-cased; \"graphql.localhost\" throws ENOTFOUND.\nThe previous commit''s *.localhost defaults were correct per Traefik''s\nown routing convention but unusable under plain Node.\n\nDefault to each service''s own direct host-port publish instead\n(services/apollo/docker-compose.yml''s 4000:4000, frontends/mfe1''s\n3001:3001) — every routed service keeps this alongside its Traefik\nroute (services/traefik/CLAUDE.md), so this sidesteps the DNS gap\nwithout losing any routing behavior, and doesn''t depend on Traefik\nbeing reachable at all for local e2e runs.\n\nVerified: e2e/test:api now passes (11/11) with zero env var\noverrides, against the same live docker-compose stack from the\nprevious commit.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): resolve release-manifest against origin/main, not local main\n\nactions/checkout with fetch-depth: 0 only populates origin/main as a\nremote-tracking ref when checking out a release/hotfix branch — the\nbare local branch main is never created, so git diff main...HEAD\nfailed with exit 128 in touchedApps().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): add missing version field to server package.json files\n\nrelease:cut reads each touched deployable app''s package.json \"version\"\nto seed its release entry — none of servers/{auth,test1,test2} had one,\nso the very first cut for this release branch failed on the first\ntouched server. frontends/*, apps/*, and root package.json already\ncarry version: \"1.0.0\"; servers were the only gap.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): grant contents:write to jobs that push commits back\n\ngithub-actions[bot] got a 403 pushing the release-manifest commit —\nthis repo''s default GITHUB_TOKEN permissions are read-only, and none\nof these three jobs (release-manifest, promote, hotfix) declared an\nexplicit permissions block, so they never had write access to begin\nwith. Scoped to just these jobs rather than flipping the repo-wide\ndefault, since none of their other steps need any broader scope.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(release): update release manifest [skip ci]\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVgSrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1xAQAEnrO3Xaf2oRAa3Xcl3FTApz\ny/hkCHis1YsxZeKb+IPwioPHNhiav2tTlKTpYkd7pmXfoIZgukQsUPAynzPxyfow\necbJrIOOqv+S/ch+g4F32YmVbtTV49Sm1yJn7FNa1Uk0x9zcXIpoiftYZ20ark0+\nKvDcMutO8+/VIjZ9mOdM4GAjLpOh8pOicmj0n5ZjoOafdgWjx3Yiy+rxZZZ2lG3t\nIFVbtjpNuE6kVUE90cUgRQrIfhtPkPHeSKXCsPWvWDvzqacEzDMabidqqT4ecEe0\nHc6lvCKe3ljEGgN9bav9zJsZwHtrfiewBTD+/Sl7CJVOTa7CzOetW+t/UZxoq2CE\ngjCKlwouC+s/kii3ErDhCEwf+Uk1XPjA1c6szekYoE0u8pubunhtFmfxhZIDzWU9\ncpmaulVrQFB4hmzGd3cJkgM8IH3+uUpfSWLdoJCHqQAIODK7FJyVyLSq8MjF7iIf\n7WvTQcDEgsGHqrdGTaXbDjkeqJIfc9QmT9ZwLebvOjnx6FGN2aa3JCUiANsjj9VR\n4f1/SKkWMyOqqUQhanBeiXVzrd9BcX41x02Cw5ZDL5PYYzrb/SbIZ/iGo6S2WD4Q\nCAKsd4n/PNZa8DMzOd3rht5Oor8agySX08Fwz9zzux8wOirhHjlkLwQJHdcqWX2d\nq+rGRNW+nlhFzeUllsiP\n=dnEu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T09:43:08Z"}},"committer":{"a