/users/kdmccormick/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kdmccormick","id":3628148,"login":"kdmccormick","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MjgxNDg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animorphixx-7/openedx-platform/commits/d91676fcb43c9d40720fd6a5a5f617b73c4e63bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-17T21:29:26Z","email":"kyle@axim.org","name":"Kyle McCormick"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-17T21:29:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Don''t look for a custom Python ZIP in Content Libs V2 (#37500)\n\nPython-evaluated problems were failing to render because they were trying to\ninvoke `course_id.make_asset_key` in order to obtain the asset key of the\ncustom Python ZIP file. Learning Core assets work differently (no asset keys,\netc.), and, furthermore, we haven''t really thought though how and whether we\nwant to support custom Python ZIPs in libraries.\n\nSo, this fix punts on supporting Python ZIP files in libraries for now, but\nenables rendering of advanced CAPA problems which don''t rely on a ZIP. This\nbrings us to parity with Legacy Libraries, which didn''t support assets at all\nand thus didn''t support Python ZIPs either.\n\nFixes: https://github.com/openedx/edx-platform/issues/37447","tree":{"sha":"9b3f115083ba410ae8a2220bcfa7161840a90087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animorphixx-7/openedx-platform/git/trees/9b3f115083ba410ae8a2220bcfa7161840a90087"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animorphixx-7/openedx-platform/git/commits/d91676fcb43c9d40720fd6a5a5f617b73c4e63bb","verification":{"payload":"tree 9b3f115083ba410ae8a2220bcfa7161840a90087\nparent e2526cfb9be7607e01aa2be590e05ddbb8051b55\nauthor Kyle McCormick <kyle@axim.org> 1760736566 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1760736566 -0400\n\nfix: Don''t look for a custom Python ZIP in Content Libs V2 (#37500)\n\nPython-evaluated problems were failing to render because they were trying to\ninvoke `course_id.make_asset_key` in order to obtain the asset key of the\ncustom Python ZIP file. Learning Core assets work differently (no asset keys,\netc.), and, furthermore, we haven''t really thought though how and whether we\nwant to support custom Python ZIPs in libraries.\n\nSo, this fix punts on supporting Python ZIP files in libraries for now, but\nenables rendering of advanced CAPA problems which don''t rely on a ZIP. This\nbrings us to parity with Legacy Libraries, which didn''t support assets at all\nand thus didn''t support Python ZIPs either.\n\nFixes: https://github.com/openedx/edx-platform/issues/37447","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJo8rU3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9ZYQAB0+PUMyvXIHT+c8/ZJFPul9\n+H6xyun8HlmvotCjOZhjgKN/DBmTBetuPHax8DlzFuOvlt4hJGPSrjXTiOsjqlum\nVM/9GpZ71qkp9H1SHz8utEyGur7QUCbNNw3uDN0mD5ZocOrgczxbQQcIRsVkW0RA\nNpKLcinLeH/L/ypvKaTwghw58kAxhMsK+VUiom2efphZWfBgPAeqcoyi6salcKUT\nSSFths6Mb64FgCKYulTLrBcWKJ2tajFvs5WmCMiSCkiAaA/mlpPP46p4zn61wASg\nZ4MmPztrwe0sVaTbfgsFJ44QMCywzsZrQigmVwt3wciWWQOWmrY7ruv2NEXH9tiF\nUN0Bhb8a+xFECWwPsUaief3zM6lGXBsDDHZOtzlCGpU/XFgGtUcIo8XRS6q9ppZ7\ntq7+90RbZ/KgjU41/otKo1mVOMJKqKB7vk1RasxKnp7WnN0ugUadR8iT6z0nDXXZ\n/t6tuhHlQpw/p5hvQLg1GmZzegWGAtsT5xdyHdDmlC+hD8pV0IWj8cbOuoK6DlGa\nLpz2Wd5Nm7mbe5uHAqQiOTAdyhVen4KYo7