cwZGMxZmViNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/UMNLibraries/primo-nde/commit/80da31849e66ac0c01dd8bb33369694aea236ae5","sha":"80da31849e66ac0c01dd8bb33369694aea236ae5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UMNLibraries/primo-nde/commits/80da31849e66ac0c01dd8bb33369694aea236ae5"}],"sha":"f614a5712ec508fae760b2ac7462d270dc1feb54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UMNLibraries/primo-nde/commits/f614a5712ec508fae760b2ac7462d270dc1feb54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1045033?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gpeterso","id":1045033,"login":"gpeterso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDUwMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpeterso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UMNLibraries/primo-nde/commits/80da31849e66ac0c01dd8bb33369694aea236ae5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T01:09:36Z","email":"1045033+gpeterso@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeff Peterson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T01:09:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Handle unexpected values in add-on config JSON (#8)\n\n* Handle bad boolean add-on config values\n\nFixes #6\n\nAbiding this behavior feels wrong, but handling the stringified\nboolean values withing the add-on is the most expedient fix.\n\n* Handle stringified maps in add-on config\n\nFixes #7\n\nIf an add-on''s config JSON contains a nested object, Primo will\nserialize the object as a \"{key=value, ...}\" string, which\nlooks as if it were Java Map.toString() output. This fix adds\nnormalization step to the HathiTrustConfigService initialization,\nbut if we add more add-ons in the future, we should consider adding\na more robust config parsing lib under shared/util/.","tree":{"sha":"7187684599fd4f850aa9a345767e863c6c8d66cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UMNLibraries/primo-nde/git/trees/7187684599fd4f850aa9a345767e863c6c8d66cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UMNLibraries/primo-nde/git/commits/80da31849e66ac0c01dd8bb33369694aea236ae5","verification":{"payload":"tree 7187684599fd4f850aa9a345767e863c6c8d66cc\nparent 081bfd8453e7f087c4bb14a5aeeea21aa336f392\nauthor Jeff Peterson <1045033+gpeterso@users.noreply.github.com> 1790298576 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790298576 -0500\n\nHandle unexpected values in add-on config JSON (#8)\n\n* Handle bad boolean add-on config values\n\nFixes #6\n\nAbiding this behavior feels wrong, but handling the stringified\nboolean values withing the add-on is the most expedient fix.\n\n* Handle stringified maps in add-on config\n\nFixes #7\n\nIf an add-on''s config JSON contains a nested object, Primo will\nserialize the object as a \"{key=value, ...}\" string, which\nlooks as if it were Java Map.toString() output. This fix adds\nnormalization step to the HathiTrustConfigService initialization,\nbut if we add more add-ons in the future, we should consider adding\na more robust config parsing lib under shared/util/.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtcnQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR4kQAKLnbNBlm+o32Noq5REWtLo0\nzmur+Rkqf7R9uzWKu3fAk0Y3aDQ2s35SrkJc8nDbmLVyVBbvcRRWUg1wvJzWfZ5l\nyjaHcFLav2D0MObSfXs3del0U1L/y0ucha3g5qLXEVcPLHqwxXWYVgRgpDRoWH9T\njpaokOY2h9slE1yCeUJ+SPiPeurJzbtnZRLgoEKFRt2oytCIaWcdu2Jtg6GbajHD\nw5m0m